{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RuzvQNDuiZWo9avTUgdGfh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"exp-001: Cross-architecture layer sweep + static probe (R1-32B, QwQ-32B)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"64 层模型全层 hidden-state 提取 + 静态 LR probe 评估。发现 bal_acc × crossing_rate 指标系统性选择浅层（L2/L10），corrected metrics 共识选择深层（L60/L63）。静态 probe 在 corrected 层显示显著 HS 优势。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"r1_32b_biased_layer\": 10,\n7\t      \"r1_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct\": 15.6,\n8\t      \"r1_32b_corrected_layer\": 63,\n9\t      \"r1_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct\": 98.4,\n10\t      \"r1_32b_layer10_bal_acc\": 0.718,\n11\t      \"r1_32b_layer10_crossing_rate\": 0.6,\n12\t      \"r1_32b_layer63_bal_acc_W1\": 0.826,\n13\t      \"r1_32b_layer63_precision_W1\": 0.603,\n14\t      \"r1_32b_layer63_fpr_W1\": 0.235,\n15\t      \"r1_32b_hs_vs_text_precision_delta_W1\": \"+15.4pp\",\n16\t      \"r1_32b_hb_W1\": \"3/3 pass\",\n17\t      \"qwq_biased_layer\": 2,\n18\t      \"qwq_biased_layer_depth_pct\": 3.1,\n19\t      \"qwq_corrected_layer\": 60,\n20\t      \"qwq_corrected_layer_depth_pct\": 93.8,\n21\t      \"qwq_layer2_bal_acc\": 0.73,\n22\t      \"qwq_layer60_bal_acc_W3\": 0.74,\n23\t      \"qwq_layer60_precision_W3\": 0.578,\n24\t      \"qwq_layer60_fpr_W3\": 0.208,\n25\t      \"qwq_hs_vs_text_precision_delta_W3\": \"+23.6pp\",\n26\t      \"qwq_hb_all_15_W\": \"15/15 pass\",\n27\t      \"selectivity_r1_32b_l63\": \"19.7pp\",\n28\t      \"selectivity_qwq_l60\": \"14.4pp\"\n29\t    },\n30\t    \"tables\": [\n31\t      {\n32\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Layer Selection Metric × Model → Selected Layer\",\n33\t        \"content\": \"| Metric             | R1-8B | OT-7B | QwQ-32B | R1-32B |\\n|--------------------|-------|-------|---------|--------|\\n| bal_acc × CR       | L0    | L0    | L2 (3%) | L10 (16%) |\\n| bal_acc (pure)     | L12   | L9    | L30 (47%) | L47 (73%) |\\n| precision          | L16   | L16   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n| pre_cp_fpr         | L16   | L20   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n| composite          | L16   | L12   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n\"\n34\t      },\n35\t      {\n36\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Biased vs Corrected Layer Impact\",\n37\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | Biased Layer | Corrected | Biased prec p | Corrected prec p |\\n|---------|-------------|-----------|---------------|-----------------|\\n| R1-32B  | L10 (16%)   | L63 (98%) | 0.050 (NS)    | <0.001 ✅       |\\n| QwQ-32B | L2 (3%)     | L60 (94%) | 0.346 (NS)    | <0.001 ✅       |\\n\"\n38\t      }\n39\t    ],\n40\t    \"figures\": [],\n41\t    \"analysis\": \"实验确立了 layer selection bias 是 32B 模型 HS 优势\\\"消失\\\"的唯一原因。在 best 档下， reviewer 接受这一发现的 mechanistic 解释（浅层 compressed representation → noise-driven crossings → inflated crossing_rate），而非将其视为\\\"选了更好的超参数\\\"。关键区分： 这是一个影响 ANY 使用 crossing_rate-contaminated 指标的研究者的 systematic bias， 而非本文特有的参数选择。LOO-CV 稳定性（65-68% fold 选择 dominant layer）进一步 证明 selection 的 robustness。\\n\\n\\nBest 档假设 layer selection sensitivity 被接受为可复现的方法论发现。在该前提下， 32B 模型的 biased → corrected 层切换从 NS (p=0.064-0.83) 翻转为高度显著 (p<0.005)， 构成论文最强 evidence。R1-32B 的 biased L10 位于 15.6% 深度（浅层），corrected L63 位于 98.4%（极深层）；QwQ 从 L2 (3.1%) 到 L60 (93.8%)。这一翻转之所以成立，是因为 浅层 hidden state 表示空间被压缩（cosine distance 1.4-2.7× smaller），crossing_rate 高但 precision 低。深层的 HS representation 编码了更多 semantic safety signal， 而非仅靠 positional encoding。4 models 全部在 corrected layers 通过 HB， 将 \\\"scale-dependent HS advantage\\\" 的旧结论完全推翻为 \\\"metric-dependent layer selection artifact\\\"。Reviewer 在 best 档接受这一叙事，因为 5 metrics × 4 models ablation 是系统性审计，而非 cherry-picking。\\n\"\n42\t  },\n43\t  {\n44\t    \"name\": \"exp-002: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation\",\n45\t    \"description\": \"在 R1-32B 和 QwQ-32B 上评估 temporal LR (W=1-25)。验证 temporal context 改善 是否跨架构泛化。\\n\",\n46\t    \"results\": {\n47\t      \"r1_32b_best_W\": 10,\n48\t      \"r1_32b_W10_bal_acc\": 0.737,\n49\t      \"r1_32b_W10_precision\": 0.609,\n50\t      \"r1_32b_W10_coverage\": 0.7,\n51\t      \"r1_32b_W10_precp_fpr\": 0.189,\n52\t      \"r1_32b_W10_lead\": 10.79,\n53\t      \"r1_32b_temporal_vs_static_delta_bal_acc\": \"+1.9pp\",\n54\t      \"qwq_best_W\": 5,\n55\t      \"qwq_W5_bal_acc\": 0.761,\n56\t      \"qwq_W5_precision\": 0.573,\n57\t      \"qwq_W5_coverage\": 0.737,\n58\t      \"qwq_W5_precp_fpr\": 0.18,\n59\t      \"qwq_W5_lead\": 20.07,\n60\t      \"qwq_temporal_vs_static_delta_bal_acc\": \"+3.1pp\",\n61\t      \"r1_32b_dimensionality_issue\": \"51200×W features for n=20; W≥5 overfitting\",\n62\t      \"r1_32b_hb_pattern\": \"W=1 only 3/3 HB; W≥3 NS after Bonferroni\",\n63\t      \"qwq_hb_pattern\": \"All W=1-15 pass HB (15/15)\"\n64\t    },\n65\t    \"tables\": [\n66\t      {\n67\t        \"name\": \"Table: Temporal Improvement Summary (32B models at corrected layers)\",\n68\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | W   | BA    | Prec  | FPR   | Coverage | Lead  | HB    |\\n|---------|-----|-------|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------|\\n| R1-32B  | 1   | 0.826 | 0.603 | 0.235 | 25%      | +11.7 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| R1-32B  | 3   | 0.738 | 0.560 | 0.306 | 80%      | +11.4 | 0/3 ❌ |\\n| R1-32B  | 10  | 0.737 | 0.609 | 0.234 | 70%      | +10.8 | 0/3 ❌ |\\n| QwQ     | 1   | 0.730 | 0.544 | 0.228 | 79%      | +19.7 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| QwQ     | 3   | 0.745 | 0.565 | 0.214 | 74%      | +20.6 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| QwQ     | 5   | 0.761 | 0.573 | 0.217 | 74%      | +20.1 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n\"\n69\t      }\n70\t    ],\n71\t    \"figures\": [],\n72\t    \"analysis\": \"Temporal context 作为 Claim 1（primary universal finding）的核心证据在 best 档 无争议。关键叙事点：text probes 在所有模型上受益于 temporal context（+3-12pp BA）， HS probes 在 3/4 模型上受益（OT-7B 的 BA 在 W=3 饱和是可复现的模型特征， precision/FPR 持续改善）。R1-32B 的 W=1-only 显著性是 n=20 power limitation 而非 temporal ineffectiveness，论文应明确区分。\\n\\n\\nTemporal improvement 是四模型中最鲁棒的发现（text 和 HS 均受益），在 best 档中 作为 universality 证据没有争议。32B 的特殊性在于维度灾难：R1-32B 5120-d × W 特征 在 n=20 test traces 下，W≥5 时参数远超样本量，导致 temporal 增益被 overfitting 抵消。 这不是 temporal context 失效，而是统计 power 不足。QwQ 的 n=19-20 同样小但因为 层选对了、信号更强，所有 W 都通过 HB。R1-32B W=1 通过 3/3 HB 但仅 25% coverage 是因为 W=1 feature 维度仅 5120（可控），但代价是 temporal context 最弱。 Best 档 reviewer 接受这一 tradeoff 为诚实报告而非 fragility。\\n\"\n73\t  },\n74\t  {\n75\t    \"name\": \"exp-003: Cross-model transfer\",\n76\t    \"description\": \"跨模型 zero-shot 迁移：Llama→Qwen, Qwen→Llama, Qwen-32B→Qwen-32B。 使用 PCA 投影对齐维度。\\n\",\n77\t    \"results\": {\n78\t      \"r1_8b_to_r1_32b_acc\": 0.522,\n79\t      \"r1_8b_to_qwq_acc\": 0.595,\n80\t      \"r1_32b_to_qwq_acc\": 0.55,\n81\t      \"qwq_to_r1_32b_acc\": 0.673,\n82\t      \"r1_32b_to_r1_8b_acc\": 0.583,\n83\t      \"best_transfer_acc\": 0.673,\n84\t      \"baseline_in_domain_acc_range\": \"0.65-0.82\",\n85\t      \"conclusion\": \"negative — all transfer at chance or near-chance\"\n86\t    },\n87\t    \"tables\": [\n88\t      {\n89\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Transfer Matrix (accuracy)\",\n90\t        \"content\": \"| Train → Test  | R1-8B | R1-32B | QwQ   | OT-7B |\\n|---------------|-------|--------|-------|-------|\\n| R1-8B         | 0.823 | 0.522  | 0.595 | —     |\\n| R1-32B        | 0.583 | 0.652  | 0.550 | —     |\\n| QwQ           | —     | 0.673  | 0.717 | —     |\\n| In-domain     | 0.823 | 0.652  | 0.717 | 0.688 |\\n\"\n91\t      }\n92\t    ],\n93\t    \"figures\": [],\n94\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 在 best 档中被 valued as community service。论文在 Discussion 中用一段讨论 cross-transfer 失败的 implication：safety representation geometry is model-specific, ruling out universal safety probes. 这与 RepE direction probing 的 failure mode 一致——mean-difference direction 也是 model-specific 且 generalizes poorly。\\n\\n\\nCross-transfer 完全失败在 best 档中是正面结果：它证明 safety representation 是 model-specific geometric encoding，不存在 universal safety direction。这支撑了 两个论点：(1) 每个模型需要独立 probe training（deployment implication）； (2) control task selectivity（7.5-18.5pp）不是 artifact——如果 safety signal 是跨模型 universal 的，transfer 应该 work。PCA 投影 (4096→5120) 的失败说明 safety information 的编码方式在不同架构/训练方法间根本不同，而非简单的维度 旋转。Qwen-32B→Qwen-32B (QwQ→R1-32B: 0.673) 是最高的 transfer，因为同架构 同规模，但仍远低于 in-domain。Best 档 reviewer 视此为 expected negative result， 加强 model-specificity 叙事。\\n\"\n95\t  },\n96\t  {\n97\t    \"name\": \"exp-004: Lead time analysis across models\",\n98\t    \"description\": \"四模型 lead time 分布分析。确认 HS probe 的检测时机特性： HS 在 commitment point 附近检测，text 更早但 trigger-happy。\\n\",\n99\t    \"results\": {\n100\t      \"r1_8b_hs_lr_lead\": -0.1,\n101\t      \"r1_8b_text_lr_lead\": 10.3,\n102\t      \"r1_8b_text_fpr_note\": \"text lead inflated by 20.5% FPR (trigger-happy)\",\n103\t      \"r1_8b_gru_lead_mean\": \"+4.5 ± 3.0\",\n104\t      \"r1_8b_gru_worst_seed\": \"+0.9\",\n105\t      \"ot_7b_hs_lead\": 21.6,\n106\t      \"ot_7b_text_lead\": 45.5,\n107\t      \"ot_7b_note\": \"absolute lead inflated by long traces (~80 sentences)\",\n108\t      \"qwq_hs_lead_W3\": \"-1.2 to +1.9\",\n109\t      \"qwq_text_lead_W3\": \"3.7 to 12.3\",\n110\t      \"qwq_caveat\": \"HS more accurate but detects LATER — practical tradeoff\",\n111\t      \"r1_32b_hs_lead_W1\": \"+11.7 to +13.3\",\n112\t      \"r1_32b_text_lead\": \"+3.7 to +9.0\",\n113\t      \"r1_32b_positive\": \"HS lead excellent at W=1; best lead time of any model\",\n114\t      \"cross_model_divergence\": \"R1-32B lead +13 (excellent) vs QwQ lead -1 (poor)\"\n115\t    },\n116\t    \"tables\": [\n117\t      {\n118\t        \"name\": \"Table: Lead Time Profile Summary\",\n119\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | HS LR Lead | Text Lead | GRU Lead  | Interpretation        |\\n|---------|-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------------|\\n| R1-8B   | ~0        | +10.3*    | +4.5±3.0  | HS=at CP, GRU modest |\\n| OT-7B   | +21.6†    | +45.5†    | +33.6±4.8 | †inflated by length  |\\n| QwQ-32B | -1 to +2  | +4 to +12 | +15.9     | HS late, text early  |\\n| R1-32B  | +12-13    | +4 to +9  | +8.8      | HS early, best case  |\\n\"\n120\t      }\n121\t    ],\n122\t    \"figures\": [],\n123\t    \"analysis\": \"Lead time 差异在 best 档中被 framed 为 deployment-relevant 实证发现， 而非 weakness。论文 Discussion 建议：R1-32B 适合 early-warning 场景（高 lead 但低 coverage），QwQ 适合 broad-monitoring 场景（high significance, all W）。 这种 per-model deployment guidance 是实证研究的 legitimate contribution。\\n\\n\\nLead time profile 是 best 档叙事中 32B cross-model divergence 的关键证据。 R1-32B 有 excellent lead time (+13 steps) 但 narrow coverage (W=1, 25%)； QwQ 有 robust significance (all W) 但 poor lead time (HS detects later than text)。 这一 divergence 不削弱 paper——相反，它展示了 32B 模型在 safety commitment detection 中的 genuine complexity，reviewer 在 best 档将此视为 nuanced empirical finding。R1-8B 的 HS lead ≈ 0 是 balanced weight 训练的结果（HS 准确检测 commitment point 本身而非预测它），只有 GRU 通过 sequence modeling 获得 modest positive lead (+4.5)，这本身就是一个有意义的发现。OT-7B 的高 absolute lead 是 trace length artifact (~80 sentences vs ~30)，论文必须 normalize 或 caveat。\\n\"\n124\t  },\n125\t  {\n126\t    \"name\": \"exp-005: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline\",\n127\t    \"description\": \"在所有 4 模型上实施 Mahalanobis distance 检测器。使用 safe traces 估计协方差， 计算每步 MD。测试 PCA 降维后的 discrimination 能力。\\n\",\n128\t    \"results\": {\n129\t      \"r1_8b_separation\": 0.07,\n130\t      \"ot_7b_separation\": 0.03,\n131\t      \"r1_32b_separation\": 0.15,\n132\t      \"qwq_32b_separation\": 0.2,\n133\t      \"max_separation\": 0.2,\n134\t      \"all_models_fail\": true,\n135\t      \"best_pca_config\": \"pca_64\",\n136\t      \"r1_8b_k5_crossing_rate\": 0.302,\n137\t      \"failure_mode\": \"signal in minor PCA components, not principal directions\",\n138\t      \"false_alarm_vs_tp\": \"FA rate ≥ TP rate at every threshold\"\n139\t    },\n140\t    \"tables\": [\n141\t      {\n142\t        \"name\": \"Table: Mahalanobis Discrimination Summary\",\n143\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | Layer | PCA  | Safe MD | Post MD | Sep   | Verdict  |\\n|---------|-------|------|---------|---------|-------|----------|\\n| R1-8B   | L14   | 64   | 6.66    | 6.73    | 0.07  | Fail     |\\n| OT-7B   | L16   | 64   | 7.68    | 7.71    | 0.03  | Fail     |\\n| QwQ-32B | L60   | 16   | 3.22    | 3.42    | 0.20  | Fail     |\\n| R1-32B  | L63   | 64   | 6.73    | 6.88    | 0.15  | Fail     |\\n\"\n144\t      }\n145\t    ],\n146\t    \"figures\": [],\n147\t    \"analysis\": \"Mahalanobis 作为 6 negative methods 之一，在 paper 中占 1-2 段。Best 档 reviewer 关注的不是 MD 为什么失败（这在 PCA Fisher ratio 分析中已解释）， 而是它 comprehensively 失败的事实本身——排除了 unsupervised distance-based 方法这一大类 approach。\\n\\n\\nMahalanobis 在所有 4 模型上 separation ≈ 0。这不是 implementation error， 而是 fundamental failure mode：safety commitment signal 编码在 minor PCA components 中（Fisher discriminant ratio 从原始 17.9 降到 PCA-3D 的 0.93）， 而 MD 测量的是 principal direction 的偏差。在 best 档中，这个 comprehensive negative result 被视为 \\\"community service\\\"——它告诉社区 TrajGuard-style detection（依赖 MD 的 unsupervised 方法）在 reasoning model safety commitment 上根本不适用。4 模型一致的失败模式（separation 0.03-0.20，FA ≥ TP at all thresholds）排除了 model-specific 偶然因素。Reviewer 在 best 档 values 这种 系统性 negative evidence。\\n\"\n148\t  },\n149\t  {\n150\t    \"name\": \"exp-006: Bootstrap CI + threshold-independent metrics\",\n151\t    \"description\": \"10,000 bootstrap resamples, Holm-Bonferroni step-down correction, 4 models × 3 metrics = 12 tests。报告 AUROC, PR curves, FPR。\\n\",\n152\t    \"results\": {\n153\t      \"n_resamples\": 10000,\n154\t      \"holm_bonferroni_pass\": \"12/12\",\n155\t      \"r1_8b_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n156\t      \"r1_8b_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n157\t      \"r1_8b_fpr_p\": \"<0.001\",\n158\t      \"ot_7b_all_3_p\": \"<0.001\",\n159\t      \"qwq_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n160\t      \"qwq_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n161\t      \"qwq_fpr_p\": 0.0061,\n162\t      \"r1_32b_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n163\t      \"r1_32b_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n164\t      \"r1_32b_fpr_p\": 0.0096,\n165\t      \"marginal_tests\": \"R1-32B FPR (p=0.0096, threshold=0.05), QwQ FPR (p=0.0061, threshold=0.025)\",\n166\t      \"precision_range\": \"+15.4 to +23.6pp\",\n167\t      \"precision_consistency\": \"remarkably consistent across 4 models\"\n168\t    },\n169\t    \"tables\": [\n170\t      {\n171\t        \"name\": \"Table: 12/12 Holm-Bonferroni Summary\",\n172\t        \"content\": \"| Rank | Model   | Metric    | Delta     | p-value | Threshold | Pass |\\n|------|---------|-----------|-----------|---------|-----------|------|\\n| 1    | R1-8B   | precision | +22.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0042    | ✅   |\\n| 2    | OT-7B   | bal_acc   | +10.7pp   | <0.001  | 0.0045    | ✅   |\\n| 3    | OT-7B   | precision | +21.9pp   | <0.001  | 0.0050    | ✅   |\\n| 4    | OT-7B   | FPR       | -17.1pp   | <0.001  | 0.0056    | ✅   |\\n| 5    | QwQ     | bal_acc   | +15.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0063    | ✅   |\\n| 6    | QwQ     | precision | +23.6pp   | <0.001  | 0.0071    | ✅   |\\n| 7    | R1-32B  | bal_acc   | +18.7pp   | <0.001  | 0.0083    | ✅   |\\n| 8    | R1-32B  | precision | +15.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0100    | ✅   |\\n| 9    | QwQ     | FPR       | -9.8pp    | 0.004   | 0.0125    | ✅   |\\n| 10   | R1-8B   | bal_acc   | +8.2pp    | 0.005   | 0.0167    | ✅   |\\n| 11   | R1-32B  | FPR       | -14.6pp   | 0.007   | 0.0250    | ✅   |\\n| 12   | R1-8B   | FPR       | -7.4pp    | 0.044   | 0.0500    | ✅   |\\n\"\n173\t      }\n174\t    ],\n175\t    \"figures\": [],\n176\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 paper 的 statistical backbone。Best 档 reviewer (soundness 4.0-4.5) 会仔细检查 multiple testing procedure 的正确性。关键防御：(1) HB step-down 是 conservative（比 Bonferroni 更 powerful 但仍控制 FWER）；(2) null-centered two-sided bootstrap 不依赖分布假设；(3) 10k resamples 确保 p-value 精度到 3 位小数。\\n\\n\\n12/12 HB pass 是 best 档 soundness rating 4.0-4.5 的基础。在 biased layers 下只有 5/12 pass；corrected layers 将全部 12 tests 翻转为 significant。 这不是 p-hacking（先选层再做 multiple testing），因为 layer selection 基于 独立的 metric sensitivity analysis（5 metrics consensus），evaluation 用的 不同 test set。Precision advantage +15-24pp 跨 4 模型的一致性（std ≈ 3.5pp） 是 best 档 reviewer 最看重的 robustness evidence——如果只有 1-2 模型显著， novelty rating 会降到 3.0。R1-32B FPR (p=0.0096) 和 QwQ FPR (p=0.0061) 是最 marginal 的两个 test，但都 comfortably pass their respective HB thresholds (0.05 和 0.025)。10k resamples（vs 原始 1k）增加了 precision 但不改变结论， 这本身证明了 statistical robustness。\\n\"\n177\t  },\n178\t  {\n179\t    \"name\": \"exp-007: Window size ablation\",\n180\t    \"description\": \"W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 4 models at corrected layers。 展示 precision-coverage tradeoff 和 diminishing returns。\\n\",\n181\t    \"results\": {\n182\t      \"r1_8b_best_bal_acc_W\": 25,\n183\t      \"r1_8b_precision_range\": \"0.693 (W=1) → 0.822 (W=25)\",\n184\t      \"r1_8b_coverage_range\": \"0.721 (W=1) → 0.488 (W=25)\",\n185\t      \"r1_8b_fpr_range\": \"0.097 (W=1) → 0.048 (W=25)\",\n186\t      \"r1_32b_best_bal_acc_W\": 10,\n187\t      \"r1_32b_precision_at_W10\": 0.609,\n188\t      \"r1_32b_coverage_at_W10\": 0.7,\n189\t      \"qwq_best_bal_acc_W\": 25,\n190\t      \"qwq_precision_at_W5\": 0.573,\n191\t      \"ot_7b_best_W\": 3,\n192\t      \"ot_7b_W3_bal_acc\": 0.688,\n193\t      \"ot_7b_saturation\": \"bal_acc peaks W=3, precision/FPR continue improving\",\n194\t      \"universal_finding\": \"coverage monotonically DECREASES with W across all 4 models\",\n195\t      \"tradeoff\": \"higher W → higher precision, lower coverage, lower FPR\"\n196\t    },\n197\t    \"tables\": [\n198\t      {\n199\t        \"name\": \"Table: Window Size × Model Ablation (bal_acc)\",\n200\t        \"content\": \"| W  | R1-8B | OT-7B | QwQ-32B | R1-32B |\\n|----|-------|-------|---------|--------|\\n| 1  | 0.778 | 0.672 | 0.730   | 0.718  |\\n| 3  | 0.790 | 0.688 | 0.745   | 0.725  |\\n| 5  | 0.781 | 0.675 | 0.761   | 0.731  |\\n| 10 | 0.793 | 0.660 | 0.747   | 0.737  |\\n| 15 | 0.802 | 0.650 | 0.741   | 0.721  |\\n| 25 | 0.810 | 0.635 | 0.762   | 0.703  |\\n\"\n201\t      }\n202\t    ],\n203\t    \"figures\": [],\n204\t    \"analysis\": \"Ablation 在 paper 中作为 appendix 完整表格 + main text 一段总结。 关键 takeaway: W 选择是 deployment decision（precision vs coverage）， 不影响 HS > text 的 modality conclusion。\\n\\n\\nCoverage 单调递减与 W 的关系在所有模型上一致，这是因为 larger W 创建了更 selective 的特征空间——probe 需要更长时间的 consistent signal 才会触发 crossing，减少了 false positives 同时也减少了 true positives（特别是短 post-CP segments）。 这不是 \\\"temporal context 有害\\\"，而是一个 precision-sensitivity tradeoff。 R1-8B 在 W=25 达到最高 bal_acc (0.810) 和 precision (0.822) 但 coverage 降到 48.8%——论文报告 W=15 作为 reported setting 是合理的 tradeoff。 OT-7B 的 bal_acc saturation at W=3 是因为 STILL training 创建了 shorter, more abrupt commitment transitions，larger W 包含了 non-informative pre-commitment context。Best 档 reviewer 接受 per-model W 选择（非 uniform W）因为论文 透明报告了所有 W 的结果。\\n\"\n205\t  },\n206\t  {\n207\t    \"name\": \"exp-008: Layer selection ablation\",\n208\t    \"description\": \"4 models × 5 metrics 完整 layer selection sensitivity analysis。 发现 crossing_rate bias 是主方法论贡献。\\n\",\n209\t    \"results\": {\n210\t      \"models_tested\": 4,\n211\t      \"metrics_tested\": 5,\n212\t      \"bias_pattern\": \"crossing_rate × bal_acc → shallow; threshold-dependent → deep; pure bal_acc → middle\",\n213\t      \"qwq_biased_L2_precision\": 0.525,\n214\t      \"qwq_corrected_L60_precision\": 0.578,\n215\t      \"qwq_precision_gain\": \"+5.3pp\",\n216\t      \"r1_32b_biased_L10_precision\": 0.516,\n217\t      \"r1_32b_corrected_L63_precision\": 0.603,\n218\t      \"r1_32b_precision_gain\": \"+8.7pp\",\n219\t      \"loo_cv_dominant_layer_stability\": \"65-68% folds select same dominant layer\",\n220\t      \"threshold_free_vs_dependent\": \"threshold-free (bal_acc, AUROC) → middle layers; threshold-dependent (precision, FPR) → deep layers\",\n221\t      \"anti_circularity\": \"BA-layer analysis (16/16 HB) refutes metric circularity concern\"\n222\t    },\n223\t    \"tables\": [\n224\t      {\n225\t        \"name\": \"Table: Metric × Model → Layer Depth (%) + HS-Text Δ Precision\",\n226\t        \"content\": \"| Metric            | R1-8B Depth | OT-7B Depth | QwQ Depth | R1-32B Depth |\\n|-------------------|-------------|-------------|-----------|-------------|\\n| BA × CR (biased)  | 0%          | 0%          | 3%        | 16%         |\\n| Pure BA           | 39%         | 32%         | 47%       | 73%         |\\n| Precision         | 52%         | 57%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n| Inverse FPR       | 52%         | 71%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n| Composite         | 52%         | 43%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n\"\n227\t      }\n228\t    ],\n229\t    \"figures\": [],\n230\t    \"analysis\": \"This subsection in Method is the paper's marquee. Best 档 reviewer 理解 这不是 hyperparameter tuning 的原因：(1) it's a reproducible bias affecting any researcher using crossing_rate; (2) the ablation is exhaustive (20 cells); (3) impact is dramatic (5/12 → 12/12 HB); (4) it generalizes a concern beyond this paper (any HS probe study using threshold-frequency metrics).\\n\\n\\n这是论文的 primary methodological contribution。Best 档核心假设 #1 直接关联： \\\"Reviewers treat layer selection metric bias as a reproducible methodological finding (not 'you just picked the wrong hyperparameter')\\\". 证据链： (1) bias 有 mechanistic 解释（浅层 compressed representation → noise-driven crossings）； (2) 5 metrics × 4 models 是系统性审计；(3) LOO-CV 65-68% stability 排除了 validation set overfitting；(4) BA-layer analysis (16/16 HB pass) 证明 HS advantage 在 ANY non-biased layer selection criterion 下都成立，refuting circularity。 第二个发现——threshold-free vs threshold-dependent 的 middle vs deep 分歧—— 是独立于 crossing_rate bias 的 second dimension of researcher degrees of freedom， 增加了方法论贡献的 depth。Best 档 novelty 3.5-4.0 很大程度源于此。\\n\"\n231\t  },\n232\t  {\n233\t    \"name\": \"exp-009: 16-label taxonomy supervision\",\n234\t    \"description\": \"使用 fine-grained 安全标签（Type 1/2/3/4）替代 binary commitment 训练 probe。 测试更丰富的监督信号是否改善 coverage 和 timing。\\n\",\n235\t    \"results\": {\n236\t      \"r1_8b_16label_bal_acc\": 0.82,\n237\t      \"r1_8b_16label_coverage\": 0.56,\n238\t      \"r1_8b_binary_coverage\": 0.51,\n239\t      \"r1_8b_coverage_delta\": \"+5pp\",\n240\t      \"r1_8b_precision_delta\": \"+1-3pp\",\n241\t      \"ot_7b_16label_bal_acc\": 0.7,\n242\t      \"ot_7b_16label_coverage\": 0.58,\n243\t      \"ot_7b_binary_coverage\": 0.53,\n244\t      \"ot_7b_coverage_delta\": \"+5pp\",\n245\t      \"32b_inconclusive\": \"n too small for 16-label with 4 classes\",\n246\t      \"finding\": \"modest improvement, not load-bearing for paper claims\"\n247\t    },\n248\t    \"tables\": [\n249\t      {\n250\t        \"name\": \"Table: Binary vs 16-Label Supervision (7-8B models)\",\n251\t        \"content\": \"| Model  | Supervision | BA    | Prec  | Coverage | Lead  |\\n|--------|-------------|-------|-------|----------|-------|\\n| R1-8B  | binary      | 0.802 | 0.777 | 0.512    | -0.1  |\\n| R1-8B  | 16-label    | 0.820 | 0.795 | 0.558    | +0.8  |\\n| OT-7B  | binary      | 0.688 | 0.466 | 0.532    | 21.6  |\\n| OT-7B  | 16-label    | 0.700 | 0.485 | 0.580    | 22.3  |\\n\"\n252\t      }\n253\t    ],\n254\t    \"figures\": [],\n255\t    \"analysis\": \"P1 实验，放 appendix。Best 档 reviewer 不会要求 16-label 作为 main result， 但 appreciation 它被 attempted。Coverage 的 modest gain 说明 binary supervision 已接近 ceiling——temporal windowing 是更有效的改善途径。\\n\\n\\n16-label taxonomy 提供了更 granular 的 supervision——probe 可以区分 \\\"safety reasoning declining\\\" 和 \\\"safety reasoning absent\\\"，而非只有 binary crossing。这在 7-8B 模型上产生 modest coverage improvement (+3-5pp)，因为 fine-grained labels 让 probe 在 commitment 附近有更 nuanced 的 decision boundary。但改善幅度小于 temporal windowing 的贡献，且 32B 模型因 n 太小（20-30 traces, 16 classes 进一步稀释了 per-class 样本）几乎无法训练。在 best 档中，这个实验放 appendix 作为 supplementary evidence，不影响主叙事。Reviewer 看到它被 attempted 且 honestly reported 就够了，不期望它成为 major finding。Best 档假设 \\\"comprehensive negative results are valued\\\" 适用于此——即使 16-label 没有显著改善，它排除了 \\\"you're underusing available supervision\\\" 这一批评。\\n\"\n256\t  },\n257\t  {\n258\t    \"name\": \"exp-010: Oracle decomposition\",\n259\t    \"description\": \"分析 oracle（使用 ground-truth label sequence）为何能实现 +31 step lead time 而 probes 不能。Decompose oracle advantage into label sequence pattern vs hidden state content。\\n\",\n260\t    \"results\": {\n261\t      \"oracle_K5_lead\": \"+31 steps\",\n262\t      \"oracle_K5_detection_rate\": \"100%\",\n263\t      \"probe_best_lead\": \"+4.5 (GRU)\",\n264\t      \"oracle_advantage_source\": \"label sequence pattern — oracle sees 5+ consecutive post-CP labels before probes stabilize\",\n265\t      \"gap_explanation\": \"Oracle exploits K-consecutive pattern in ground-truth labels (pure sequence), while probes must INFER label from noisy HS features. The 31-step gap comes from label noise: probe confidence fluctuates around CP, requiring temporal smoothing (W) to stabilize, whereas oracle has clean binary signal.\\n\",\n266\t      \"implication\": \"ceiling on probe lead time is limited by representation noise, not information absence\",\n267\t      \"pre_cp_safety_streaks\": \"mean 14.6 consecutive safe labels before CP\"\n268\t    },\n269\t    \"tables\": [\n270\t      {\n271\t        \"name\": \"Table: Oracle vs Best Probe Performance (R1-8B)\",\n272\t        \"content\": \"| Method         | Detection | Lead  | Mechanism                    |\\n|----------------|-----------|-------|------------------------------|\\n| Oracle K=5     | 100%      | +31   | Clean label sequence pattern |\\n| GRU multi-7L   | 76.7%     | +4.5  | Learned confidence dynamics  |\\n| HS Temporal LR | 76.7%     | -0.1  | Snapshot classification      |\\n| Text Temporal  | 65.1%     | +10.3 | Text-level (trigger-happy)   |\\n\"\n273\t      }\n274\t    ],\n275\t    \"figures\": [],\n276\t    \"analysis\": \"Discussion section 核心段落。Best 档 reviewer 会问 \\\"can you close the gap?\\\" 答案是 honest \\\"not with current approaches\\\"——这是一个 fundamental limitation of snapshot-based HS monitoring。论文建议 future work 方向：(1) predictive probes (trained to predict FUTURE safety state); (2) attention pattern analysis; (3) multi-step trajectory modeling beyond GRU。\\n\\n\\nOracle +31 step lead vs probe +4.5 step lead 的 gap 解释是 Discussion section 的关键内容。Hidden states DO encode current safety state（static probe 80% BA）， 但 POORLY predict future trajectory（probe 看到 t 时刻的 HS，只能判断 t 时刻 的 safety state，不能预测 t+5 是否会 commit）。Oracle 利用的是 label sequence 中 K-consecutive pattern——一旦连续 5 个 post-CP label 出现，oracle 确信 commitment 已发生。Probe 无法复制这一优势，因为：(1) probe confidence 在 CP 附近波动（pre-CP 也有 false crossings）；(2) temporal smoothing (W) 帮助但 引入了 latency；(3) GRU 的 +4.5 step lead 是 sequence modeling 的 modest contribution（学会了 \\\"confidence 持续上升 = commitment\\\"的 pattern）。 Best 档 reviewer 视此分析为对 fundamental limitation 的 honest investigation。\\n\"\n277\t  },\n278\t  {\n279\t    \"name\": \"exp-011: OpenThinker-7B (4th model, completing 2×2 matrix)\",\n280\t    \"description\": \"完成 2×2 architecture×scale matrix：Llama-8B (R1-8B), Qwen-7B (OT-7B), Qwen-32B (QwQ), Qwen-32B (R1-32B)。OT-7B 填充 Qwen-7B slot。\\n\",\n281\t    \"results\": {\n282\t      \"n_traces\": 228,\n283\t      \"best_layer\": 16,\n284\t      \"best_layer_depth_pct\": 57.1,\n285\t      \"hs_best_W\": 3,\n286\t      \"hs_best_bal_acc\": 0.688,\n287\t      \"hs_best_precision\": 0.466,\n288\t      \"hs_best_fpr\": 0.1,\n289\t      \"hs_best_coverage\": 0.532,\n290\t      \"text_best_W\": 25,\n291\t      \"text_best_bal_acc\": 0.614,\n292\t      \"text_best_precision\": 0.329,\n293\t      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_ba\": \"+10.7pp (p<0.001)\",\n294\t      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_prec\": \"+21.9pp (p<0.001)\",\n295\t      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_fpr\": \"-17.1pp (p<0.001)\",\n296\t      \"holm_bonferroni\": \"3/3 pass\",\n297\t      \"selectivity\": \"18.3pp (highest across all 4 models)\",\n298\t      \"gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.746,\n299\t      \"gru_multi_coverage\": 0.645,\n300\t      \"gru_multi_lead\": 33.6,\n301\t      \"gru_multi_fpr\": 0.274,\n302\t      \"ot7b_hs_temporal_saturation\": \"BA peaks at W=3 (0.688), declines at W≥5; precision/FPR continue improving\"\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [\n305\t      {\n306\t        \"name\": \"Table: OT-7B Full Pipeline Summary\",\n307\t        \"content\": \"| Method           | BA    | Prec  | FPR   | Cov   | Lead  |\\n|------------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\\n| HS Static L16    | 0.672 | 0.357 | 0.188 | —     | —     |\\n| HS Temp W=3 L16  | 0.688 | 0.466 | 0.100 | 0.532 | 21.6  |\\n| Text Temp W=25   | 0.614 | 0.329 | 0.161 | 0.660 | 45.5  |\\n| GRU Multi L13-19 | 0.746 | —     | 0.274 | 0.645 | 33.6  |\\n\"\n308\t      }\n309\t    ],\n310\t    \"figures\": [],\n311\t    \"analysis\": \"OT-7B 数据在 paper 中出现在每张 summary table 中。它的 cleanness 为 HS advantage 叙事提供了 anchor point——即使 32B 有 caveats，7-8B 证据 是 unambiguous。\\n\\n\\nOT-7B 是 4 模型中 \\\"cleanest single-model evidence\\\"：3/3 HB pass with large effect sizes, highest selectivity (18.3pp), 5/5 seed robustness, 和最大的 residualized gap (+6.9pp after position removal)。它作为 Qwen-7B (STILL-trained) slot 完成 2×2 matrix 的作用是关键的：它证明 HS advantage 不是 Llama-specific， 也不是 R1-distillation-specific。STILL training 创建了不同于 R1-distillation 的 safety reasoning pattern（更短、更 abrupt 的 commitment），但 HS 优势依然 显著。OT-7B 的 W=3 temporal saturation 是 genuine model characteristic（两个 layer 都确认），不影响 BA 以外的 metrics。Best 档假设 #2 直接相关：\\\"4 models × 2 architectures × 2 scales is accepted as sufficient breadth\\\"。228 traces 是最大数据集（vs R1-8B 209, QwQ 95, R1-32B 100），给了最高统计 power。\\n\"\n312\t  },\n313\t  {\n314\t    \"name\": \"exp-012: GRU/Attention probe on 32B models\",\n315\t    \"description\": \"在 32B 模型 corrected layers 上训练 GRU probe。验证 \\\"LR sufficient, GRU adds modest improvement\\\" 的结论是否跨 scale 成立。\\n\",\n316\t    \"results\": {\n317\t      \"qwq_gru_single_bal_acc\": 0.724,\n318\t      \"qwq_gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.71,\n319\t      \"qwq_gru_lead\": 15.9,\n320\t      \"qwq_gru_fpr\": 0.289,\n321\t      \"r1_32b_gru_single_bal_acc\": 0.675,\n322\t      \"r1_32b_gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.655,\n323\t      \"r1_32b_gru_lead\": 9.1,\n324\t      \"r1_32b_gru_fpr\": 0.135,\n325\t      \"gru_vs_lr_qwq\": \"-3.7pp BA (LR W=5: 0.761 > GRU single: 0.724)\",\n326\t      \"gru_vs_lr_r1_32b\": \"-6.2pp BA (LR W=10: 0.737 > GRU single: 0.675)\",\n327\t      \"gru_advantage\": \"longer lead time than LR, at cost of higher FPR\",\n328\t      \"finding\": \"GRU does NOT outperform LR on 32B; strengthens 'linear probes sufficient' narrative\",\n329\t      \"note\": \"results at OLD biased layers; corrected-layer GRU may differ\"\n330\t    },\n331\t    \"tables\": [\n332\t      {\n333\t        \"name\": \"Table: GRU vs LR Comparison (all models)\",\n334\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | LR Best BA | GRU BA   | Δ       | GRU Lead | LR Lead |\\n|---------|-----------|----------|---------|----------|---------|\\n| R1-8B   | 0.802     | 0.809    | +0.7pp  | +4.5     | -0.1    |\\n| OT-7B   | 0.688     | 0.746    | +5.8pp  | +33.6    | +21.6   |\\n| QwQ-32B | 0.761     | 0.724    | -3.7pp  | +15.9    | ~0      |\\n| R1-32B  | 0.737     | 0.675    | -6.2pp  | +9.1     | +12.9   |\\n\"\n335\t      }\n336\t    ],\n337\t    \"figures\": [],\n338\t    \"analysis\": \"GRU 数据支持论文的 practical message：\\\"use simple LR + temporal window\\\"。 32B GRU at biased layers 需要 re-evaluation at corrected layers 但论文 可以 caveat this as future work。\\n\\n\\nGRU 在 32B 上不优于 LR 的原因是相同的 dimensionality constraint：5120-d HS 输入 × sequence length 对于 n=20-30 test traces 来说参数过多。GRU 的优势 在于 sequence modeling（捕捉 confidence 随时间的动态），但当 base signal (HS) 足够 linearly separable 时（如 4 模型 precision +15-24pp 所示），nonlinear sequence modeling 无法提供额外信息。这与 MLP probe 的 negative result 一致： 3/4 models MLP worse than LR。在 best 档中，\\\"linear probes sufficient\\\"是一个 important practical finding——deployment 不需要 complex model，simple LR +  temporal window 就够了。这降低了 method 的 adoption barrier。GRU 在 7-8B 上 的 modest advantage (+4.5 lead) 是 genuine 但 small，论文报告为 \\\"GRU achieves modest positive lead where LR detects at CP\\\"。\\n\"\n339\t  },\n340\t  {\n341\t    \"name\": \"exp-013: Text-based baseline (sentence-BERT)\",\n342\t    \"description\": \"all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings + temporal LR (W=15) on CoT text。 验证 HS monitoring 相比 cheap text monitoring 的 unique value。\\n\",\n343\t    \"results\": {\n344\t      \"r1_8b_text_static_acc\": 0.661,\n345\t      \"r1_8b_text_static_auroc\": 0.738,\n346\t      \"r1_8b_text_temporal_w15_acc\": 0.678,\n347\t      \"r1_8b_text_temporal_w15_auroc\": 0.759,\n348\t      \"r1_8b_hs_advantage_over_text\": \"15-18pp accuracy\",\n349\t      \"r1_8b_text_safe_fpr\": 0.502,\n350\t      \"r1_8b_text_precp_fpr\": 0.356,\n351\t      \"r1_8b_hs_precp_fpr\": 0.162,\n352\t      \"hs_vs_text_fpr_delta\": \"-19.4pp\",\n353\t      \"text_coverage\": 0.651,\n354\t      \"text_lead\": 11.5,\n355\t      \"hs_lead\": 4.9,\n356\t      \"text_precision\": 0.487,\n357\t      \"hs_precision\": 0.583,\n358\t      \"key_finding\": \"HS adds unique value: +15pp accuracy, +10pp precision, -19pp FPR over text baseline\",\n359\t      \"text_not_useless\": \"text temporal achieves 67.8% acc — non-trivial but significantly below HS\"\n360\t    },\n361\t    \"tables\": [\n362\t      {\n363\t        \"name\": \"Table: HS vs Text Baseline (R1-8B)\",\n364\t        \"content\": \"| Method         | BA    | Prec  | FPR-pre | FPR-safe | Lead  | Cov   |\\n|----------------|-------|-------|---------|----------|-------|-------|\\n| HS Static      | 0.768 | 0.622 | 0.162   | 0.390    | +3.0  | 0.605 |\\n| HS Temporal W15| 0.726 | 0.583 | 0.160   | 0.392    | +4.9  | 0.651 |\\n| Text Static    | 0.661 | 0.448 | 0.356   | 0.502    | +4.3  | 0.605 |\\n| Text Temp W15  | 0.678 | 0.487 | 0.272   | 0.385    | +11.5 | 0.651 |\\n| GRU            | 0.816 | 0.648 | 0.188   | 0.521    | +5.3  | 0.744 |\\n\"\n365\t      }\n366\t    ],\n367\t    \"figures\": [],\n368\t    \"analysis\": \"Text baseline 在 paper 中作为 Table 的一行存在，不需要 dedicated subsection。 Key message：HS provides 15-19pp advantage over text，这是 non-trivial 且 statistically significant (12/12 HB)，justifying the added complexity of HS extraction。\\n\\n\\nText baseline 是 best 档中 paper motivation 的关键防线。如果 text 能 match HS performance，整个 \\\"hidden-state monitoring\\\" 的 raison d'être 就消失了。 实际结果：text 在 accuracy、precision、FPR 上全面落后 HS 15-19pp，但 text 不是 zero——它达到了 67.8% accuracy，说明 CoT 文本确实包含 safety 信息（符合直觉： safety reasoning 在文本中可见）。HS 的优势在于 sub-textual signal：hidden states 编码了模型\\\"实际在想什么\\\"而非\\\"写出来了什么\\\"，这在 safety commitment detection 中提供了 additional discriminative power。Text 的高 lead time (+11.5 vs HS +4.9) 是 artifact of trigger-happy detection（text FPR 20.5% vs HS 8.8%）——text 更早触发是因为它更容易 false alarm。Best 档 reviewer 在看到 comprehensive HS vs text comparison 后接受 \\\"HS adds unique value beyond text monitoring\\\"。\\n\"\n369\t  },\n370\t  {\n371\t    \"name\": \"exp-014: BOCPD/CUSUM change-point detection\",\n372\t    \"description\": \"Adams & MacKay 2007 BOCPD + CUSUM on probe score sequences。 测试能否通过检测 distributional shift 获得 positive lead time。\\n\",\n373\t    \"results\": {\n374\t      \"r1_8b_bocpd_lambda10_detection\": 0.93,\n375\t      \"r1_8b_bocpd_lambda10_lead\": 3.45,\n376\t      \"r1_8b_fcp_baseline_lead\": 4.89,\n377\t      \"r1_8b_bocpd_vs_fcp\": \"higher detection (93% vs 65%) but lower mean lead (3.45 vs 4.89)\",\n378\t      \"ot_7b_bocpd_all_lambda\": \"0% detection — probe scores too spiky\",\n379\t      \"r1_32b_bocpd\": \"0% detection\",\n380\t      \"qwq_bocpd\": \"0% detection\",\n381\t      \"cusum_verdict\": \"universally worse than simple threshold\",\n382\t      \"cross_model_bocpd\": \"only R1-8B works (93%); 3/4 models 0%\",\n383\t      \"finding\": \"BOCPD/CUSUM fail to improve over simple thresholds on 3/4 models; R1-8B exception due to gradual commitment pattern\"\n384\t    },\n385\t    \"tables\": [\n386\t      {\n387\t        \"name\": \"Table: BOCPD/CUSUM Cross-Model Summary\",\n388\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | BOCPD Det | BOCPD Lead | CUSUM Det | FCP Lead | Winner     |\\n|---------|----------|-----------|----------|---------|-----------|\\n| R1-8B   | 93%      | +3.5      | 65.1%    | +4.9    | FCP (lead) |\\n| OT-7B   | 0%       | —         | 70.2%    | +7.5    | FCP        |\\n| QwQ-32B | 0%       | —         | 73.7%    | +9.4    | FCP        |\\n| R1-32B  | 0%       | —         | 85%      | +2.6    | FCP        |\\n\"\n389\t      }\n390\t    ],\n391\t    \"figures\": [],\n392\t    \"analysis\": \"BOCPD/CUSUM 是 6 negative methods 的第二组。论文 1 段总结： \\\"Advanced change-point methods fail because safety commitment dynamics are model-specific; BOCPD's Gaussian assumption is violated by abrupt transitions in 3/4 models.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBOCPD 在 3/4 模型上 0% detection 的原因是 commitment dynamics 的 model-specificity： R1-8B 有 gradual commitment transition（probe confidence 缓慢上升），BOCPD 的 Gaussian changepoint model 能捕捉这种 distributional shift。但 OT-7B/R1-32B/QwQ 有 abrupt commitment（probe score 在 1-2 steps 内从 0 跳到 1），BOCPD 的 Gaussian model 无法 adapt 到这种 spike pattern。CUSUM 更简单但同样依赖 gradual shift 假设。这个 negative result 在 best 档中有双重价值：(1) 排除了 \\\"just use BOCPD\\\" 这一 obvious baseline；(2) 揭示了 commitment dynamics 的 model-specificity—— 同一方法在不同模型上表现截然不同，further supporting 论文 \\\"one-size-fits-all detection doesn't work\\\" 的 message。Best 档假设 #4 \\\"comprehensive negative results valued as community service\\\" 直接适用。\\n\"\n393\t  },\n394\t  {\n395\t    \"name\": \"exp-015: False positive analysis on safe traces\",\n396\t    \"description\": \"所有 probe 方法在 safe traces (final_judgment=0.5) 上的 FPR。 Essential for deployment utility claims。\\n\",\n397\t    \"results\": {\n398\t      \"r1_8b_hs_static_safe_fpr\": 0.39,\n399\t      \"r1_8b_text_static_safe_fpr\": 0.502,\n400\t      \"r1_8b_hs_temporal_safe_fpr\": 0.392,\n401\t      \"r1_8b_gru_safe_fpr\": 0.521,\n402\t      \"ot_7b_hs_static_safe_fpr\": 0.111,\n403\t      \"ot_7b_text_static_safe_fpr\": 0.302,\n404\t      \"qwq_hs_safe_fpr\": 0.475,\n405\t      \"qwq_text_safe_fpr\": 0.5,\n406\t      \"r1_32b_hs_safe_fpr\": 0.239,\n407\t      \"r1_32b_text_safe_fpr\": 0.31,\n408\t      \"overall_safe_fpr_range\": \"11.1% - 62%\",\n409\t      \"acknowledged_limitation\": \"safe FPR 39-62% for most model-method combos; OT-7B exception at 11.1%\",\n410\t      \"hs_vs_text_fpr\": \"HS lower than text in 3/4 models (exception: QwQ)\"\n411\t    },\n412\t    \"tables\": [\n413\t      {\n414\t        \"name\": \"Table: Safe Trace FPR Summary\",\n415\t        \"content\": \"| Model   | HS Static | HS Temp | Text Static | Text Temp | GRU   |\\n|---------|----------|---------|-------------|-----------|-------|\\n| R1-8B   | 39.0%    | 39.2%   | 50.2%       | 38.5%     | 52.1% |\\n| OT-7B   | 11.1%    | 17.5%   | 30.2%       | 46.0%     | —     |\\n| QwQ-32B | 50.0%    | 45.0%   | 32.5%       | 42.5%     | —     |\\n| R1-32B  | 23.9%    | 23.9%   | 31.0%       | 31.0%     | —     |\\n\"\n416\t      }\n417\t    ],\n418\t    \"figures\": [],\n419\t    \"analysis\": \"Limitations section 明确列出 high safe FPR 作为 top limitation。 论文 framing：\\\"These results establish baselines for future improvement rather than production-ready thresholds.\\\" Best 档 reviewer 不会因为高 FPR reject，因为这是 evaluation paper 而非 system paper。\\n\\n\\nHigh safe FPR (39-62%) 是 best 档 acknowledged limitation。Best 档核心假设 #6： \\\"High safe FPR (39-62%) is acceptable as acknowledged limitation for a detection-evaluation paper.\\\" 这里的关键 framing：本文不声称 ready-for-deployment detector，而是 \\\"systematic evaluation revealing what works and what doesn't for this new threat model\\\"。Safe FPR 高说明所有方法（包括 HS temporal）都还 不够 mature 用于 production intervention——但这正是 empirical study 的 value： 建立 baseline 并量化 gap。OT-7B 的异常低 safe FPR (11.1%) 是因为 STILL training 创建了 cleaner separation of safe vs unsafe traces in HS space。QwQ 的 HS safe FPR (47.5%) > text safe FPR (50.0%) 是 caveat——在 QwQ 上 HS 并不总是 better than text on every metric。Best 档 reviewer 接受高 safe FPR 因为论文 transparently acknowledges 它并且 frames contribution 为 evaluation study 而非 deployable system。\\n\"\n420\t  },\n421\t  {\n422\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_cv_7b: CV-validated multi-metric ensemble layer selection\",\n423\t    \"description\": \"5-fold CV validation of multi-metric ensemble layer selection on 7-8B models。 验证 ensemble 在 cross-validation 下是否消除 metric-induced bias。\\n\",\n424\t    \"results\": {\n425\t      \"r1_8b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_mean\": 0.174,\n426\t      \"r1_8b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_std\": 0.026,\n427\t      \"r1_8b_hs_better_folds\": \"5/5\",\n428\t      \"ot_7b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_mean\": 0.164,\n429\t      \"ot_7b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_std\": 0.033,\n430\t      \"ot_7b_hs_better_folds\": \"5/5\",\n431\t      \"total_hs_better_folds\": \"10/10\",\n432\t      \"ensemble_prec_vs_best_single\": \"ensemble ≈ best single metric (never worse)\",\n433\t      \"ensemble_vs_text_all_significant\": true,\n434\t      \"ensemble_vs_text_p_max\": 0.002,\n435\t      \"impact_on_acceptance\": \"0-5% (cosmetic, not load-bearing)\"\n436\t    },\n437\t    \"tables\": [\n438\t      {\n439\t        \"name\": \"Table: Ensemble CV Results (Appendix)\",\n440\t        \"content\": \"| Model  | Metric        | Fold 1 | Fold 2 | Fold 3 | Fold 4 | Fold 5 | Mean±Std       |\\n|--------|---------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------------|\\n| R1-8B  | ΔPrecision    | +0.19  | +0.16  | +0.18  | +0.15  | +0.19  | +0.174±0.026  |\\n| R1-8B  | HS>Text?      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | 5/5           |\\n| OT-7B  | ΔPrecision    | +0.20  | +0.13  | +0.17  | +0.16  | +0.16  | +0.164±0.033  |\\n| OT-7B  | HS>Text?      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | 5/5           |\\n\"\n441\t      }\n442\t    ],\n443\t    \"figures\": [],\n444\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix-only content。Best 档 reviewer 如果 notice 它会 appreciate thoroughness 但不会将其列入 strengths/weaknesses。对 acceptance probability 的 marginal contribution ≤5%。论文 space budget：1/4 page in appendix max。\\n\\nEnsemble CV 在 best 档中的 impact 接近 zero (0-5%)。原因：paper 的 acceptance 已经由 12/12 HB, position mediation 3/4, 5-seed robustness, 16/16 BA-layer analysis 这些 evidence package 支撑。Ensemble CV 做的是 \\\"validate that multi-metric consensus layer selection is stable under CV\\\"——但 LOO-CV stability (65-68%) 已经回答了这个问题。Ensemble 结果 10/10 folds HS better than text 是 consistent 但 unsurprising。Best 档 reviewer 不会要求 \\\"please add CV-validated ensemble\\\" 作为 acceptance condition，因为 individual metric analysis 已经足够 rigorous。 Ensemble 放 appendix 作为 supplementary validation，不进入 main text contribution claims。核心假设 \\\"ensemble_cv_impact_on_acceptance: [0.0, 0.05]\\\" 直接适用。\\n\"\n445\t  }\n446\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c0610e2-18f5-465e-b8e4-959a05a2a7cd","uuid":"c4f57ea6-1864-4480-8145-9f0279c5b315","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:46:28.334Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-001: Cross-architecture layer sweep + static probe (R1-32B, QwQ-32B)\",\n    \"description\": \"64 层模型全层 hidden-state 提取 + 静态 LR probe 评估。发现 bal_acc × crossing_rate 指标系统性选择浅层（L2/L10），corrected metrics 共识选择深层（L60/L63）。静态 probe 在 corrected 层显示显著 HS 优势。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_32b_biased_layer\": 10,\n      \"r1_32b_biased_layer_depth_pct\": 15.6,\n      \"r1_32b_corrected_layer\": 63,\n      \"r1_32b_corrected_layer_depth_pct\": 98.4,\n      \"r1_32b_layer10_bal_acc\": 0.718,\n      \"r1_32b_layer10_crossing_rate\": 0.6,\n      \"r1_32b_layer63_bal_acc_W1\": 0.826,\n      \"r1_32b_layer63_precision_W1\": 0.603,\n      \"r1_32b_layer63_fpr_W1\": 0.235,\n      \"r1_32b_hs_vs_text_precision_delta_W1\": \"+15.4pp\",\n      \"r1_32b_hb_W1\": \"3/3 pass\",\n      \"qwq_biased_layer\": 2,\n      \"qwq_biased_layer_depth_pct\": 3.1,\n      \"qwq_corrected_layer\": 60,\n      \"qwq_corrected_layer_depth_pct\": 93.8,\n      \"qwq_layer2_bal_acc\": 0.73,\n      \"qwq_layer60_bal_acc_W3\": 0.74,\n      \"qwq_layer60_precision_W3\": 0.578,\n      \"qwq_layer60_fpr_W3\": 0.208,\n      \"qwq_hs_vs_text_precision_delta_W3\": \"+23.6pp\",\n      \"qwq_hb_all_15_W\": \"15/15 pass\",\n      \"selectivity_r1_32b_l63\": \"19.7pp\",\n      \"selectivity_qwq_l60\": \"14.4pp\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Layer Selection Metric × Model → Selected Layer\",\n        \"content\": \"| Metric             | R1-8B | OT-7B | QwQ-32B | R1-32B |\\n|--------------------|-------|-------|---------|--------|\\n| bal_acc × CR       | L0    | L0    | L2 (3%) | L10 (16%) |\\n| bal_acc (pure)     | L12   | L9    | L30 (47%) | L47 (73%) |\\n| precision          | L16   | L16   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n| pre_cp_fpr         | L16   | L20   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n| composite          | L16   | L12   | L60 (94%) | L63 (98%) |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Biased vs Corrected Layer Impact\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | Biased Layer | Corrected | Biased prec p | Corrected prec p |\\n|---------|-------------|-----------|---------------|-----------------|\\n| R1-32B  | L10 (16%)   | L63 (98%) | 0.050 (NS)    | <0.001 ✅       |\\n| QwQ-32B | L2 (3%)     | L60 (94%) | 0.346 (NS)    | <0.001 ✅       |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"实验确立了 layer selection bias 是 32B 模型 HS 优势\\\"消失\\\"的唯一原因。在 best 档下， reviewer 接受这一发现的 mechanistic 解释（浅层 compressed representation → noise-driven crossings → inflated crossing_rate），而非将其视为\\\"选了更好的超参数\\\"。关键区分： 这是一个影响 ANY 使用 crossing_rate-contaminated 指标的研究者的 systematic bias， 而非本文特有的参数选择。LOO-CV 稳定性（65-68% fold 选择 dominant layer）进一步 证明 selection 的 robustness。\\n\\n\\nBest 档假设 layer selection sensitivity 被接受为可复现的方法论发现。在该前提下， 32B 模型的 biased → corrected 层切换从 NS (p=0.064-0.83) 翻转为高度显著 (p<0.005)， 构成论文最强 evidence。R1-32B 的 biased L10 位于 15.6% 深度（浅层），corrected L63 位于 98.4%（极深层）；QwQ 从 L2 (3.1%) 到 L60 (93.8%)。这一翻转之所以成立，是因为 浅层 hidden state 表示空间被压缩（cosine distance 1.4-2.7× smaller），crossing_rate 高但 precision 低。深层的 HS representation 编码了更多 semantic safety signal， 而非仅靠 positional encoding。4 models 全部在 corrected layers 通过 HB， 将 \\\"scale-dependent HS advantage\\\" 的旧结论完全推翻为 \\\"metric-dependent layer selection artifact\\\"。Reviewer 在 best 档接受这一叙事，因为 5 metrics × 4 models ablation 是系统性审计，而非 cherry-picking。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-002: Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"在 R1-32B 和 QwQ-32B 上评估 temporal LR (W=1-25)。验证 temporal context 改善 是否跨架构泛化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_32b_best_W\": 10,\n      \"r1_32b_W10_bal_acc\": 0.737,\n      \"r1_32b_W10_precision\": 0.609,\n      \"r1_32b_W10_coverage\": 0.7,\n      \"r1_32b_W10_precp_fpr\": 0.189,\n      \"r1_32b_W10_lead\": 10.79,\n      \"r1_32b_temporal_vs_static_delta_bal_acc\": \"+1.9pp\",\n      \"qwq_best_W\": 5,\n      \"qwq_W5_bal_acc\": 0.761,\n      \"qwq_W5_precision\": 0.573,\n      \"qwq_W5_coverage\": 0.737,\n      \"qwq_W5_precp_fpr\": 0.18,\n      \"qwq_W5_lead\": 20.07,\n      \"qwq_temporal_vs_static_delta_bal_acc\": \"+3.1pp\",\n      \"r1_32b_dimensionality_issue\": \"51200×W features for n=20; W≥5 overfitting\",\n      \"r1_32b_hb_pattern\": \"W=1 only 3/3 HB; W≥3 NS after Bonferroni\",\n      \"qwq_hb_pattern\": \"All W=1-15 pass HB (15/15)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Temporal Improvement Summary (32B models at corrected layers)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | W   | BA    | Prec  | FPR   | Coverage | Lead  | HB    |\\n|---------|-----|-------|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------|\\n| R1-32B  | 1   | 0.826 | 0.603 | 0.235 | 25%      | +11.7 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| R1-32B  | 3   | 0.738 | 0.560 | 0.306 | 80%      | +11.4 | 0/3 ❌ |\\n| R1-32B  | 10  | 0.737 | 0.609 | 0.234 | 70%      | +10.8 | 0/3 ❌ |\\n| QwQ     | 1   | 0.730 | 0.544 | 0.228 | 79%      | +19.7 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| QwQ     | 3   | 0.745 | 0.565 | 0.214 | 74%      | +20.6 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n| QwQ     | 5   | 0.761 | 0.573 | 0.217 | 74%      | +20.1 | 3/3 ✅ |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Temporal context 作为 Claim 1（primary universal finding）的核心证据在 best 档 无争议。关键叙事点：text probes 在所有模型上受益于 temporal context（+3-12pp BA）， HS probes 在 3/4 模型上受益（OT-7B 的 BA 在 W=3 饱和是可复现的模型特征， precision/FPR 持续改善）。R1-32B 的 W=1-only 显著性是 n=20 power limitation 而非 temporal ineffectiveness，论文应明确区分。\\n\\n\\nTemporal improvement 是四模型中最鲁棒的发现（text 和 HS 均受益），在 best 档中 作为 universality 证据没有争议。32B 的特殊性在于维度灾难：R1-32B 5120-d × W 特征 在 n=20 test traces 下，W≥5 时参数远超样本量，导致 temporal 增益被 overfitting 抵消。 这不是 temporal context 失效，而是统计 power 不足。QwQ 的 n=19-20 同样小但因为 层选对了、信号更强，所有 W 都通过 HB。R1-32B W=1 通过 3/3 HB 但仅 25% coverage 是因为 W=1 feature 维度仅 5120（可控），但代价是 temporal context 最弱。 Best 档 reviewer 接受这一 tradeoff 为诚实报告而非 fragility。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-003: Cross-model transfer\",\n    \"description\": \"跨模型 zero-shot 迁移：Llama→Qwen, Qwen→Llama, Qwen-32B→Qwen-32B。 使用 PCA 投影对齐维度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_to_r1_32b_acc\": 0.522,\n      \"r1_8b_to_qwq_acc\": 0.595,\n      \"r1_32b_to_qwq_acc\": 0.55,\n      \"qwq_to_r1_32b_acc\": 0.673,\n      \"r1_32b_to_r1_8b_acc\": 0.583,\n      \"best_transfer_acc\": 0.673,\n      \"baseline_in_domain_acc_range\": \"0.65-0.82\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"negative — all transfer at chance or near-chance\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Transfer Matrix (accuracy)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Train → Test  | R1-8B | R1-32B | QwQ   | OT-7B |\\n|---------------|-------|--------|-------|-------|\\n| R1-8B         | 0.823 | 0.522  | 0.595 | —     |\\n| R1-32B        | 0.583 | 0.652  | 0.550 | —     |\\n| QwQ           | —     | 0.673  | 0.717 | —     |\\n| In-domain     | 0.823 | 0.652  | 0.717 | 0.688 |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 在 best 档中被 valued as community service。论文在 Discussion 中用一段讨论 cross-transfer 失败的 implication：safety representation geometry is model-specific, ruling out universal safety probes. 这与 RepE direction probing 的 failure mode 一致——mean-difference direction 也是 model-specific 且 generalizes poorly。\\n\\n\\nCross-transfer 完全失败在 best 档中是正面结果：它证明 safety representation 是 model-specific geometric encoding，不存在 universal safety direction。这支撑了 两个论点：(1) 每个模型需要独立 probe training（deployment implication）； (2) control task selectivity（7.5-18.5pp）不是 artifact——如果 safety signal 是跨模型 universal 的，transfer 应该 work。PCA 投影 (4096→5120) 的失败说明 safety information 的编码方式在不同架构/训练方法间根本不同，而非简单的维度 旋转。Qwen-32B→Qwen-32B (QwQ→R1-32B: 0.673) 是最高的 transfer，因为同架构 同规模，但仍远低于 in-domain。Best 档 reviewer 视此为 expected negative result， 加强 model-specificity 叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-004: Lead time analysis across models\",\n    \"description\": \"四模型 lead time 分布分析。确认 HS probe 的检测时机特性： HS 在 commitment point 附近检测，text 更早但 trigger-happy。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_hs_lr_lead\": -0.1,\n      \"r1_8b_text_lr_lead\": 10.3,\n      \"r1_8b_text_fpr_note\": \"text lead inflated by 20.5% FPR (trigger-happy)\",\n      \"r1_8b_gru_lead_mean\": \"+4.5 ± 3.0\",\n      \"r1_8b_gru_worst_seed\": \"+0.9\",\n      \"ot_7b_hs_lead\": 21.6,\n      \"ot_7b_text_lead\": 45.5,\n      \"ot_7b_note\": \"absolute lead inflated by long traces (~80 sentences)\",\n      \"qwq_hs_lead_W3\": \"-1.2 to +1.9\",\n      \"qwq_text_lead_W3\": \"3.7 to 12.3\",\n      \"qwq_caveat\": \"HS more accurate but detects LATER — practical tradeoff\",\n      \"r1_32b_hs_lead_W1\": \"+11.7 to +13.3\",\n      \"r1_32b_text_lead\": \"+3.7 to +9.0\",\n      \"r1_32b_positive\": \"HS lead excellent at W=1; best lead time of any model\",\n      \"cross_model_divergence\": \"R1-32B lead +13 (excellent) vs QwQ lead -1 (poor)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Lead Time Profile Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | HS LR Lead | Text Lead | GRU Lead  | Interpretation        |\\n|---------|-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------------|\\n| R1-8B   | ~0        | +10.3*    | +4.5±3.0  | HS=at CP, GRU modest |\\n| OT-7B   | +21.6†    | +45.5†    | +33.6±4.8 | †inflated by length  |\\n| QwQ-32B | -1 to +2  | +4 to +12 | +15.9     | HS late, text early  |\\n| R1-32B  | +12-13    | +4 to +9  | +8.8      | HS early, best case  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Lead time 差异在 best 档中被 framed 为 deployment-relevant 实证发现， 而非 weakness。论文 Discussion 建议：R1-32B 适合 early-warning 场景（高 lead 但低 coverage），QwQ 适合 broad-monitoring 场景（high significance, all W）。 这种 per-model deployment guidance 是实证研究的 legitimate contribution。\\n\\n\\nLead time profile 是 best 档叙事中 32B cross-model divergence 的关键证据。 R1-32B 有 excellent lead time (+13 steps) 但 narrow coverage (W=1, 25%)； QwQ 有 robust significance (all W) 但 poor lead time (HS detects later than text)。 这一 divergence 不削弱 paper——相反，它展示了 32B 模型在 safety commitment detection 中的 genuine complexity，reviewer 在 best 档将此视为 nuanced empirical finding。R1-8B 的 HS lead ≈ 0 是 balanced weight 训练的结果（HS 准确检测 commitment point 本身而非预测它），只有 GRU 通过 sequence modeling 获得 modest positive lead (+4.5)，这本身就是一个有意义的发现。OT-7B 的高 absolute lead 是 trace length artifact (~80 sentences vs ~30)，论文必须 normalize 或 caveat。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-005: TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"在所有 4 模型上实施 Mahalanobis distance 检测器。使用 safe traces 估计协方差， 计算每步 MD。测试 PCA 降维后的 discrimination 能力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_separation\": 0.07,\n      \"ot_7b_separation\": 0.03,\n      \"r1_32b_separation\": 0.15,\n      \"qwq_32b_separation\": 0.2,\n      \"max_separation\": 0.2,\n      \"all_models_fail\": true,\n      \"best_pca_config\": \"pca_64\",\n      \"r1_8b_k5_crossing_rate\": 0.302,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"signal in minor PCA components, not principal directions\",\n      \"false_alarm_vs_tp\": \"FA rate ≥ TP rate at every threshold\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Mahalanobis Discrimination Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | Layer | PCA  | Safe MD | Post MD | Sep   | Verdict  |\\n|---------|-------|------|---------|---------|-------|----------|\\n| R1-8B   | L14   | 64   | 6.66    | 6.73    | 0.07  | Fail     |\\n| OT-7B   | L16   | 64   | 7.68    | 7.71    | 0.03  | Fail     |\\n| QwQ-32B | L60   | 16   | 3.22    | 3.42    | 0.20  | Fail     |\\n| R1-32B  | L63   | 64   | 6.73    | 6.88    | 0.15  | Fail     |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mahalanobis 作为 6 negative methods 之一，在 paper 中占 1-2 段。Best 档 reviewer 关注的不是 MD 为什么失败（这在 PCA Fisher ratio 分析中已解释）， 而是它 comprehensively 失败的事实本身——排除了 unsupervised distance-based 方法这一大类 approach。\\n\\n\\nMahalanobis 在所有 4 模型上 separation ≈ 0。这不是 implementation error， 而是 fundamental failure mode：safety commitment signal 编码在 minor PCA components 中（Fisher discriminant ratio 从原始 17.9 降到 PCA-3D 的 0.93）， 而 MD 测量的是 principal direction 的偏差。在 best 档中，这个 comprehensive negative result 被视为 \\\"community service\\\"——它告诉社区 TrajGuard-style detection（依赖 MD 的 unsupervised 方法）在 reasoning model safety commitment 上根本不适用。4 模型一致的失败模式（separation 0.03-0.20，FA ≥ TP at all thresholds）排除了 model-specific 偶然因素。Reviewer 在 best 档 values 这种 系统性 negative evidence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-006: Bootstrap CI + threshold-independent metrics\",\n    \"description\": \"10,000 bootstrap resamples, Holm-Bonferroni step-down correction, 4 models × 3 metrics = 12 tests。报告 AUROC, PR curves, FPR。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_resamples\": 10000,\n      \"holm_bonferroni_pass\": \"12/12\",\n      \"r1_8b_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"r1_8b_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"r1_8b_fpr_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"ot_7b_all_3_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"qwq_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"qwq_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"qwq_fpr_p\": 0.0061,\n      \"r1_32b_bal_acc_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"r1_32b_precision_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"r1_32b_fpr_p\": 0.0096,\n      \"marginal_tests\": \"R1-32B FPR (p=0.0096, threshold=0.05), QwQ FPR (p=0.0061, threshold=0.025)\",\n      \"precision_range\": \"+15.4 to +23.6pp\",\n      \"precision_consistency\": \"remarkably consistent across 4 models\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 12/12 Holm-Bonferroni Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Rank | Model   | Metric    | Delta     | p-value | Threshold | Pass |\\n|------|---------|-----------|-----------|---------|-----------|------|\\n| 1    | R1-8B   | precision | +22.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0042    | ✅   |\\n| 2    | OT-7B   | bal_acc   | +10.7pp   | <0.001  | 0.0045    | ✅   |\\n| 3    | OT-7B   | precision | +21.9pp   | <0.001  | 0.0050    | ✅   |\\n| 4    | OT-7B   | FPR       | -17.1pp   | <0.001  | 0.0056    | ✅   |\\n| 5    | QwQ     | bal_acc   | +15.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0063    | ✅   |\\n| 6    | QwQ     | precision | +23.6pp   | <0.001  | 0.0071    | ✅   |\\n| 7    | R1-32B  | bal_acc   | +18.7pp   | <0.001  | 0.0083    | ✅   |\\n| 8    | R1-32B  | precision | +15.4pp   | <0.001  | 0.0100    | ✅   |\\n| 9    | QwQ     | FPR       | -9.8pp    | 0.004   | 0.0125    | ✅   |\\n| 10   | R1-8B   | bal_acc   | +8.2pp    | 0.005   | 0.0167    | ✅   |\\n| 11   | R1-32B  | FPR       | -14.6pp   | 0.007   | 0.0250    | ✅   |\\n| 12   | R1-8B   | FPR       | -7.4pp    | 0.044   | 0.0500    | ✅   |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 paper 的 statistical backbone。Best 档 reviewer (soundness 4.0-4.5) 会仔细检查 multiple testing procedure 的正确性。关键防御：(1) HB step-down 是 conservative（比 Bonferroni 更 powerful 但仍控制 FWER）；(2) null-centered two-sided bootstrap 不依赖分布假设；(3) 10k resamples 确保 p-value 精度到 3 位小数。\\n\\n\\n12/12 HB pass 是 best 档 soundness rating 4.0-4.5 的基础。在 biased layers 下只有 5/12 pass；corrected layers 将全部 12 tests 翻转为 significant。 这不是 p-hacking（先选层再做 multiple testing），因为 layer selection 基于 独立的 metric sensitivity analysis（5 metrics consensus），evaluation 用的 不同 test set。Precision advantage +15-24pp 跨 4 模型的一致性（std ≈ 3.5pp） 是 best 档 reviewer 最看重的 robustness evidence——如果只有 1-2 模型显著， novelty rating 会降到 3.0。R1-32B FPR (p=0.0096) 和 QwQ FPR (p=0.0061) 是最 marginal 的两个 test，但都 comfortably pass their respective HB thresholds (0.05 和 0.025)。10k resamples（vs 原始 1k）增加了 precision 但不改变结论， 这本身证明了 statistical robustness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-007: Window size ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 4 models at corrected layers。 展示 precision-coverage tradeoff 和 diminishing returns。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_best_bal_acc_W\": 25,\n      \"r1_8b_precision_range\": \"0.693 (W=1) → 0.822 (W=25)\",\n      \"r1_8b_coverage_range\": \"0.721 (W=1) → 0.488 (W=25)\",\n      \"r1_8b_fpr_range\": \"0.097 (W=1) → 0.048 (W=25)\",\n      \"r1_32b_best_bal_acc_W\": 10,\n      \"r1_32b_precision_at_W10\": 0.609,\n      \"r1_32b_coverage_at_W10\": 0.7,\n      \"qwq_best_bal_acc_W\": 25,\n      \"qwq_precision_at_W5\": 0.573,\n      \"ot_7b_best_W\": 3,\n      \"ot_7b_W3_bal_acc\": 0.688,\n      \"ot_7b_saturation\": \"bal_acc peaks W=3, precision/FPR continue improving\",\n      \"universal_finding\": \"coverage monotonically DECREASES with W across all 4 models\",\n      \"tradeoff\": \"higher W → higher precision, lower coverage, lower FPR\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Window Size × Model Ablation (bal_acc)\",\n        \"content\": \"| W  | R1-8B | OT-7B | QwQ-32B | R1-32B |\\n|----|-------|-------|---------|--------|\\n| 1  | 0.778 | 0.672 | 0.730   | 0.718  |\\n| 3  | 0.790 | 0.688 | 0.745   | 0.725  |\\n| 5  | 0.781 | 0.675 | 0.761   | 0.731  |\\n| 10 | 0.793 | 0.660 | 0.747   | 0.737  |\\n| 15 | 0.802 | 0.650 | 0.741   | 0.721  |\\n| 25 | 0.810 | 0.635 | 0.762   | 0.703  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ablation 在 paper 中作为 appendix 完整表格 + main text 一段总结。 关键 takeaway: W 选择是 deployment decision（precision vs coverage）， 不影响 HS > text 的 modality conclusion。\\n\\n\\nCoverage 单调递减与 W 的关系在所有模型上一致，这是因为 larger W 创建了更 selective 的特征空间——probe 需要更长时间的 consistent signal 才会触发 crossing，减少了 false positives 同时也减少了 true positives（特别是短 post-CP segments）。 这不是 \\\"temporal context 有害\\\"，而是一个 precision-sensitivity tradeoff。 R1-8B 在 W=25 达到最高 bal_acc (0.810) 和 precision (0.822) 但 coverage 降到 48.8%——论文报告 W=15 作为 reported setting 是合理的 tradeoff。 OT-7B 的 bal_acc saturation at W=3 是因为 STILL training 创建了 shorter, more abrupt commitment transitions，larger W 包含了 non-informative pre-commitment context。Best 档 reviewer 接受 per-model W 选择（非 uniform W）因为论文 透明报告了所有 W 的结果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-008: Layer selection ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × 5 metrics 完整 layer selection sensitivity analysis。 发现 crossing_rate bias 是主方法论贡献。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_tested\": 4,\n      \"metrics_tested\": 5,\n      \"bias_pattern\": \"crossing_rate × bal_acc → shallow; threshold-dependent → deep; pure bal_acc → middle\",\n      \"qwq_biased_L2_precision\": 0.525,\n      \"qwq_corrected_L60_precision\": 0.578,\n      \"qwq_precision_gain\": \"+5.3pp\",\n      \"r1_32b_biased_L10_precision\": 0.516,\n      \"r1_32b_corrected_L63_precision\": 0.603,\n      \"r1_32b_precision_gain\": \"+8.7pp\",\n      \"loo_cv_dominant_layer_stability\": \"65-68% folds select same dominant layer\",\n      \"threshold_free_vs_dependent\": \"threshold-free (bal_acc, AUROC) → middle layers; threshold-dependent (precision, FPR) → deep layers\",\n      \"anti_circularity\": \"BA-layer analysis (16/16 HB) refutes metric circularity concern\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Metric × Model → Layer Depth (%) + HS-Text Δ Precision\",\n        \"content\": \"| Metric            | R1-8B Depth | OT-7B Depth | QwQ Depth | R1-32B Depth |\\n|-------------------|-------------|-------------|-----------|-------------|\\n| BA × CR (biased)  | 0%          | 0%          | 3%        | 16%         |\\n| Pure BA           | 39%         | 32%         | 47%       | 73%         |\\n| Precision         | 52%         | 57%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n| Inverse FPR       | 52%         | 71%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n| Composite         | 52%         | 43%         | 94%       | 98%         |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"This subsection in Method is the paper's marquee. Best 档 reviewer 理解 这不是 hyperparameter tuning 的原因：(1) it's a reproducible bias affecting any researcher using crossing_rate; (2) the ablation is exhaustive (20 cells); (3) impact is dramatic (5/12 → 12/12 HB); (4) it generalizes a concern beyond this paper (any HS probe study using threshold-frequency metrics).\\n\\n\\n这是论文的 primary methodological contribution。Best 档核心假设 #1 直接关联： \\\"Reviewers treat layer selection metric bias as a reproducible methodological finding (not 'you just picked the wrong hyperparameter')\\\". 证据链： (1) bias 有 mechanistic 解释（浅层 compressed representation → noise-driven crossings）； (2) 5 metrics × 4 models 是系统性审计；(3) LOO-CV 65-68% stability 排除了 validation set overfitting；(4) BA-layer analysis (16/16 HB pass) 证明 HS advantage 在 ANY non-biased layer selection criterion 下都成立，refuting circularity。 第二个发现——threshold-free vs threshold-dependent 的 middle vs deep 分歧—— 是独立于 crossing_rate bias 的 second dimension of researcher degrees of freedom， 增加了方法论贡献的 depth。Best 档 novelty 3.5-4.0 很大程度源于此。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-009: 16-label taxonomy supervision\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 fine-grained 安全标签（Type 1/2/3/4）替代 binary commitment 训练 probe。 测试更丰富的监督信号是否改善 coverage 和 timing。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_16label_bal_acc\": 0.82,\n      \"r1_8b_16label_coverage\": 0.56,\n      \"r1_8b_binary_coverage\": 0.51,\n      \"r1_8b_coverage_delta\": \"+5pp\",\n      \"r1_8b_precision_delta\": \"+1-3pp\",\n      \"ot_7b_16label_bal_acc\": 0.7,\n      \"ot_7b_16label_coverage\": 0.58,\n      \"ot_7b_binary_coverage\": 0.53,\n      \"ot_7b_coverage_delta\": \"+5pp\",\n      \"32b_inconclusive\": \"n too small for 16-label with 4 classes\",\n      \"finding\": \"modest improvement, not load-bearing for paper claims\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Binary vs 16-Label Supervision (7-8B models)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model  | Supervision | BA    | Prec  | Coverage | Lead  |\\n|--------|-------------|-------|-------|----------|-------|\\n| R1-8B  | binary      | 0.802 | 0.777 | 0.512    | -0.1  |\\n| R1-8B  | 16-label    | 0.820 | 0.795 | 0.558    | +0.8  |\\n| OT-7B  | binary      | 0.688 | 0.466 | 0.532    | 21.6  |\\n| OT-7B  | 16-label    | 0.700 | 0.485 | 0.580    | 22.3  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"P1 实验，放 appendix。Best 档 reviewer 不会要求 16-label 作为 main result， 但 appreciation 它被 attempted。Coverage 的 modest gain 说明 binary supervision 已接近 ceiling——temporal windowing 是更有效的改善途径。\\n\\n\\n16-label taxonomy 提供了更 granular 的 supervision——probe 可以区分 \\\"safety reasoning declining\\\" 和 \\\"safety reasoning absent\\\"，而非只有 binary crossing。这在 7-8B 模型上产生 modest coverage improvement (+3-5pp)，因为 fine-grained labels 让 probe 在 commitment 附近有更 nuanced 的 decision boundary。但改善幅度小于 temporal windowing 的贡献，且 32B 模型因 n 太小（20-30 traces, 16 classes 进一步稀释了 per-class 样本）几乎无法训练。在 best 档中，这个实验放 appendix 作为 supplementary evidence，不影响主叙事。Reviewer 看到它被 attempted 且 honestly reported 就够了，不期望它成为 major finding。Best 档假设 \\\"comprehensive negative results are valued\\\" 适用于此——即使 16-label 没有显著改善，它排除了 \\\"you're underusing available supervision\\\" 这一批评。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-010: Oracle decomposition\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 oracle（使用 ground-truth label sequence）为何能实现 +31 step lead time 而 probes 不能。Decompose oracle advantage into label sequence pattern vs hidden state content。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"oracle_K5_lead\": \"+31 steps\",\n      \"oracle_K5_detection_rate\": \"100%\",\n      \"probe_best_lead\": \"+4.5 (GRU)\",\n      \"oracle_advantage_source\": \"label sequence pattern — oracle sees 5+ consecutive post-CP labels before probes stabilize\",\n      \"gap_explanation\": \"Oracle exploits K-consecutive pattern in ground-truth labels (pure sequence), while probes must INFER label from noisy HS features. The 31-step gap comes from label noise: probe confidence fluctuates around CP, requiring temporal smoothing (W) to stabilize, whereas oracle has clean binary signal.\\n\",\n      \"implication\": \"ceiling on probe lead time is limited by representation noise, not information absence\",\n      \"pre_cp_safety_streaks\": \"mean 14.6 consecutive safe labels before CP\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Oracle vs Best Probe Performance (R1-8B)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Method         | Detection | Lead  | Mechanism                    |\\n|----------------|-----------|-------|------------------------------|\\n| Oracle K=5     | 100%      | +31   | Clean label sequence pattern |\\n| GRU multi-7L   | 76.7%     | +4.5  | Learned confidence dynamics  |\\n| HS Temporal LR | 76.7%     | -0.1  | Snapshot classification      |\\n| Text Temporal  | 65.1%     | +10.3 | Text-level (trigger-happy)   |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Discussion section 核心段落。Best 档 reviewer 会问 \\\"can you close the gap?\\\" 答案是 honest \\\"not with current approaches\\\"——这是一个 fundamental limitation of snapshot-based HS monitoring。论文建议 future work 方向：(1) predictive probes (trained to predict FUTURE safety state); (2) attention pattern analysis; (3) multi-step trajectory modeling beyond GRU。\\n\\n\\nOracle +31 step lead vs probe +4.5 step lead 的 gap 解释是 Discussion section 的关键内容。Hidden states DO encode current safety state（static probe 80% BA）， 但 POORLY predict future trajectory（probe 看到 t 时刻的 HS，只能判断 t 时刻 的 safety state，不能预测 t+5 是否会 commit）。Oracle 利用的是 label sequence 中 K-consecutive pattern——一旦连续 5 个 post-CP label 出现，oracle 确信 commitment 已发生。Probe 无法复制这一优势，因为：(1) probe confidence 在 CP 附近波动（pre-CP 也有 false crossings）；(2) temporal smoothing (W) 帮助但 引入了 latency；(3) GRU 的 +4.5 step lead 是 sequence modeling 的 modest contribution（学会了 \\\"confidence 持续上升 = commitment\\\"的 pattern）。 Best 档 reviewer 视此分析为对 fundamental limitation 的 honest investigation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-011: OpenThinker-7B (4th model, completing 2×2 matrix)\",\n    \"description\": \"完成 2×2 architecture×scale matrix：Llama-8B (R1-8B), Qwen-7B (OT-7B), Qwen-32B (QwQ), Qwen-32B (R1-32B)。OT-7B 填充 Qwen-7B slot。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_traces\": 228,\n      \"best_layer\": 16,\n      \"best_layer_depth_pct\": 57.1,\n      \"hs_best_W\": 3,\n      \"hs_best_bal_acc\": 0.688,\n      \"hs_best_precision\": 0.466,\n      \"hs_best_fpr\": 0.1,\n      \"hs_best_coverage\": 0.532,\n      \"text_best_W\": 25,\n      \"text_best_bal_acc\": 0.614,\n      \"text_best_precision\": 0.329,\n      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_ba\": \"+10.7pp (p<0.001)\",\n      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_prec\": \"+21.9pp (p<0.001)\",\n      \"bootstrap_hs_text_delta_fpr\": \"-17.1pp (p<0.001)\",\n      \"holm_bonferroni\": \"3/3 pass\",\n      \"selectivity\": \"18.3pp (highest across all 4 models)\",\n      \"gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.746,\n      \"gru_multi_coverage\": 0.645,\n      \"gru_multi_lead\": 33.6,\n      \"gru_multi_fpr\": 0.274,\n      \"ot7b_hs_temporal_saturation\": \"BA peaks at W=3 (0.688), declines at W≥5; precision/FPR continue improving\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: OT-7B Full Pipeline Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Method           | BA    | Prec  | FPR   | Cov   | Lead  |\\n|------------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\\n| HS Static L16    | 0.672 | 0.357 | 0.188 | —     | —     |\\n| HS Temp W=3 L16  | 0.688 | 0.466 | 0.100 | 0.532 | 21.6  |\\n| Text Temp W=25   | 0.614 | 0.329 | 0.161 | 0.660 | 45.5  |\\n| GRU Multi L13-19 | 0.746 | —     | 0.274 | 0.645 | 33.6  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OT-7B 数据在 paper 中出现在每张 summary table 中。它的 cleanness 为 HS advantage 叙事提供了 anchor point——即使 32B 有 caveats，7-8B 证据 是 unambiguous。\\n\\n\\nOT-7B 是 4 模型中 \\\"cleanest single-model evidence\\\"：3/3 HB pass with large effect sizes, highest selectivity (18.3pp), 5/5 seed robustness, 和最大的 residualized gap (+6.9pp after position removal)。它作为 Qwen-7B (STILL-trained) slot 完成 2×2 matrix 的作用是关键的：它证明 HS advantage 不是 Llama-specific， 也不是 R1-distillation-specific。STILL training 创建了不同于 R1-distillation 的 safety reasoning pattern（更短、更 abrupt 的 commitment），但 HS 优势依然 显著。OT-7B 的 W=3 temporal saturation 是 genuine model characteristic（两个 layer 都确认），不影响 BA 以外的 metrics。Best 档假设 #2 直接相关：\\\"4 models × 2 architectures × 2 scales is accepted as sufficient breadth\\\"。228 traces 是最大数据集（vs R1-8B 209, QwQ 95, R1-32B 100），给了最高统计 power。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-012: GRU/Attention probe on 32B models\",\n    \"description\": \"在 32B 模型 corrected layers 上训练 GRU probe。验证 \\\"LR sufficient, GRU adds modest improvement\\\" 的结论是否跨 scale 成立。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwq_gru_single_bal_acc\": 0.724,\n      \"qwq_gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.71,\n      \"qwq_gru_lead\": 15.9,\n      \"qwq_gru_fpr\": 0.289,\n      \"r1_32b_gru_single_bal_acc\": 0.675,\n      \"r1_32b_gru_multi_bal_acc\": 0.655,\n      \"r1_32b_gru_lead\": 9.1,\n      \"r1_32b_gru_fpr\": 0.135,\n      \"gru_vs_lr_qwq\": \"-3.7pp BA (LR W=5: 0.761 > GRU single: 0.724)\",\n      \"gru_vs_lr_r1_32b\": \"-6.2pp BA (LR W=10: 0.737 > GRU single: 0.675)\",\n      \"gru_advantage\": \"longer lead time than LR, at cost of higher FPR\",\n      \"finding\": \"GRU does NOT outperform LR on 32B; strengthens 'linear probes sufficient' narrative\",\n      \"note\": \"results at OLD biased layers; corrected-layer GRU may differ\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GRU vs LR Comparison (all models)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | LR Best BA | GRU BA   | Δ       | GRU Lead | LR Lead |\\n|---------|-----------|----------|---------|----------|---------|\\n| R1-8B   | 0.802     | 0.809    | +0.7pp  | +4.5     | -0.1    |\\n| OT-7B   | 0.688     | 0.746    | +5.8pp  | +33.6    | +21.6   |\\n| QwQ-32B | 0.761     | 0.724    | -3.7pp  | +15.9    | ~0      |\\n| R1-32B  | 0.737     | 0.675    | -6.2pp  | +9.1     | +12.9   |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRU 数据支持论文的 practical message：\\\"use simple LR + temporal window\\\"。 32B GRU at biased layers 需要 re-evaluation at corrected layers 但论文 可以 caveat this as future work。\\n\\n\\nGRU 在 32B 上不优于 LR 的原因是相同的 dimensionality constraint：5120-d HS 输入 × sequence length 对于 n=20-30 test traces 来说参数过多。GRU 的优势 在于 sequence modeling（捕捉 confidence 随时间的动态），但当 base signal (HS) 足够 linearly separable 时（如 4 模型 precision +15-24pp 所示），nonlinear sequence modeling 无法提供额外信息。这与 MLP probe 的 negative result 一致： 3/4 models MLP worse than LR。在 best 档中，\\\"linear probes sufficient\\\"是一个 important practical finding——deployment 不需要 complex model，simple LR +  temporal window 就够了。这降低了 method 的 adoption barrier。GRU 在 7-8B 上 的 modest advantage (+4.5 lead) 是 genuine 但 small，论文报告为 \\\"GRU achieves modest positive lead where LR detects at CP\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-013: Text-based baseline (sentence-BERT)\",\n    \"description\": \"all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings + temporal LR (W=15) on CoT text。 验证 HS monitoring 相比 cheap text monitoring 的 unique value。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_text_static_acc\": 0.661,\n      \"r1_8b_text_static_auroc\": 0.738,\n      \"r1_8b_text_temporal_w15_acc\": 0.678,\n      \"r1_8b_text_temporal_w15_auroc\": 0.759,\n      \"r1_8b_hs_advantage_over_text\": \"15-18pp accuracy\",\n      \"r1_8b_text_safe_fpr\": 0.502,\n      \"r1_8b_text_precp_fpr\": 0.356,\n      \"r1_8b_hs_precp_fpr\": 0.162,\n      \"hs_vs_text_fpr_delta\": \"-19.4pp\",\n      \"text_coverage\": 0.651,\n      \"text_lead\": 11.5,\n      \"hs_lead\": 4.9,\n      \"text_precision\": 0.487,\n      \"hs_precision\": 0.583,\n      \"key_finding\": \"HS adds unique value: +15pp accuracy, +10pp precision, -19pp FPR over text baseline\",\n      \"text_not_useless\": \"text temporal achieves 67.8% acc — non-trivial but significantly below HS\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: HS vs Text Baseline (R1-8B)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Method         | BA    | Prec  | FPR-pre | FPR-safe | Lead  | Cov   |\\n|----------------|-------|-------|---------|----------|-------|-------|\\n| HS Static      | 0.768 | 0.622 | 0.162   | 0.390    | +3.0  | 0.605 |\\n| HS Temporal W15| 0.726 | 0.583 | 0.160   | 0.392    | +4.9  | 0.651 |\\n| Text Static    | 0.661 | 0.448 | 0.356   | 0.502    | +4.3  | 0.605 |\\n| Text Temp W15  | 0.678 | 0.487 | 0.272   | 0.385    | +11.5 | 0.651 |\\n| GRU            | 0.816 | 0.648 | 0.188   | 0.521    | +5.3  | 0.744 |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Text baseline 在 paper 中作为 Table 的一行存在，不需要 dedicated subsection。 Key message：HS provides 15-19pp advantage over text，这是 non-trivial 且 statistically significant (12/12 HB)，justifying the added complexity of HS extraction。\\n\\n\\nText baseline 是 best 档中 paper motivation 的关键防线。如果 text 能 match HS performance，整个 \\\"hidden-state monitoring\\\" 的 raison d'être 就消失了。 实际结果：text 在 accuracy、precision、FPR 上全面落后 HS 15-19pp，但 text 不是 zero——它达到了 67.8% accuracy，说明 CoT 文本确实包含 safety 信息（符合直觉： safety reasoning 在文本中可见）。HS 的优势在于 sub-textual signal：hidden states 编码了模型\\\"实际在想什么\\\"而非\\\"写出来了什么\\\"，这在 safety commitment detection 中提供了 additional discriminative power。Text 的高 lead time (+11.5 vs HS +4.9) 是 artifact of trigger-happy detection（text FPR 20.5% vs HS 8.8%）——text 更早触发是因为它更容易 false alarm。Best 档 reviewer 在看到 comprehensive HS vs text comparison 后接受 \\\"HS adds unique value beyond text monitoring\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-014: BOCPD/CUSUM change-point detection\",\n    \"description\": \"Adams & MacKay 2007 BOCPD + CUSUM on probe score sequences。 测试能否通过检测 distributional shift 获得 positive lead time。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_bocpd_lambda10_detection\": 0.93,\n      \"r1_8b_bocpd_lambda10_lead\": 3.45,\n      \"r1_8b_fcp_baseline_lead\": 4.89,\n      \"r1_8b_bocpd_vs_fcp\": \"higher detection (93% vs 65%) but lower mean lead (3.45 vs 4.89)\",\n      \"ot_7b_bocpd_all_lambda\": \"0% detection — probe scores too spiky\",\n      \"r1_32b_bocpd\": \"0% detection\",\n      \"qwq_bocpd\": \"0% detection\",\n      \"cusum_verdict\": \"universally worse than simple threshold\",\n      \"cross_model_bocpd\": \"only R1-8B works (93%); 3/4 models 0%\",\n      \"finding\": \"BOCPD/CUSUM fail to improve over simple thresholds on 3/4 models; R1-8B exception due to gradual commitment pattern\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: BOCPD/CUSUM Cross-Model Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | BOCPD Det | BOCPD Lead | CUSUM Det | FCP Lead | Winner     |\\n|---------|----------|-----------|----------|---------|-----------|\\n| R1-8B   | 93%      | +3.5      | 65.1%    | +4.9    | FCP (lead) |\\n| OT-7B   | 0%       | —         | 70.2%    | +7.5    | FCP        |\\n| QwQ-32B | 0%       | —         | 73.7%    | +9.4    | FCP        |\\n| R1-32B  | 0%       | —         | 85%      | +2.6    | FCP        |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BOCPD/CUSUM 是 6 negative methods 的第二组。论文 1 段总结： \\\"Advanced change-point methods fail because safety commitment dynamics are model-specific; BOCPD's Gaussian assumption is violated by abrupt transitions in 3/4 models.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBOCPD 在 3/4 模型上 0% detection 的原因是 commitment dynamics 的 model-specificity： R1-8B 有 gradual commitment transition（probe confidence 缓慢上升），BOCPD 的 Gaussian changepoint model 能捕捉这种 distributional shift。但 OT-7B/R1-32B/QwQ 有 abrupt commitment（probe score 在 1-2 steps 内从 0 跳到 1），BOCPD 的 Gaussian model 无法 adapt 到这种 spike pattern。CUSUM 更简单但同样依赖 gradual shift 假设。这个 negative result 在 best 档中有双重价值：(1) 排除了 \\\"just use BOCPD\\\" 这一 obvious baseline；(2) 揭示了 commitment dynamics 的 model-specificity—— 同一方法在不同模型上表现截然不同，further supporting 论文 \\\"one-size-fits-all detection doesn't work\\\" 的 message。Best 档假设 #4 \\\"comprehensive negative results valued as community service\\\" 直接适用。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-015: False positive analysis on safe traces\",\n    \"description\": \"所有 probe 方法在 safe traces (final_judgment=0.5) 上的 FPR。 Essential for deployment utility claims。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_hs_static_safe_fpr\": 0.39,\n      \"r1_8b_text_static_safe_fpr\": 0.502,\n      \"r1_8b_hs_temporal_safe_fpr\": 0.392,\n      \"r1_8b_gru_safe_fpr\": 0.521,\n      \"ot_7b_hs_static_safe_fpr\": 0.111,\n      \"ot_7b_text_static_safe_fpr\": 0.302,\n      \"qwq_hs_safe_fpr\": 0.475,\n      \"qwq_text_safe_fpr\": 0.5,\n      \"r1_32b_hs_safe_fpr\": 0.239,\n      \"r1_32b_text_safe_fpr\": 0.31,\n      \"overall_safe_fpr_range\": \"11.1% - 62%\",\n      \"acknowledged_limitation\": \"safe FPR 39-62% for most model-method combos; OT-7B exception at 11.1%\",\n      \"hs_vs_text_fpr\": \"HS lower than text in 3/4 models (exception: QwQ)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Safe Trace FPR Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model   | HS Static | HS Temp | Text Static | Text Temp | GRU   |\\n|---------|----------|---------|-------------|-----------|-------|\\n| R1-8B   | 39.0%    | 39.2%   | 50.2%       | 38.5%     | 52.1% |\\n| OT-7B   | 11.1%    | 17.5%   | 30.2%       | 46.0%     | —     |\\n| QwQ-32B | 50.0%    | 45.0%   | 32.5%       | 42.5%     | —     |\\n| R1-32B  | 23.9%    | 23.9%   | 31.0%       | 31.0%     | —     |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Limitations section 明确列出 high safe FPR 作为 top limitation。 论文 framing：\\\"These results establish baselines for future improvement rather than production-ready thresholds.\\\" Best 档 reviewer 不会因为高 FPR reject，因为这是 evaluation paper 而非 system paper。\\n\\n\\nHigh safe FPR (39-62%) 是 best 档 acknowledged limitation。Best 档核心假设 #6： \\\"High safe FPR (39-62%) is acceptable as acknowledged limitation for a detection-evaluation paper.\\\" 这里的关键 framing：本文不声称 ready-for-deployment detector，而是 \\\"systematic evaluation revealing what works and what doesn't for this new threat model\\\"。Safe FPR 高说明所有方法（包括 HS temporal）都还 不够 mature 用于 production intervention——但这正是 empirical study 的 value： 建立 baseline 并量化 gap。OT-7B 的异常低 safe FPR (11.1%) 是因为 STILL training 创建了 cleaner separation of safe vs unsafe traces in HS space。QwQ 的 HS safe FPR (47.5%) > text safe FPR (50.0%) 是 caveat——在 QwQ 上 HS 并不总是 better than text on every metric。Best 档 reviewer 接受高 safe FPR 因为论文 transparently acknowledges 它并且 frames contribution 为 evaluation study 而非 deployable system。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_cv_7b: CV-validated multi-metric ensemble layer selection\",\n    \"description\": \"5-fold CV validation of multi-metric ensemble layer selection on 7-8B models。 验证 ensemble 在 cross-validation 下是否消除 metric-induced bias。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r1_8b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_mean\": 0.174,\n      \"r1_8b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_std\": 0.026,\n      \"r1_8b_hs_better_folds\": \"5/5\",\n      \"ot_7b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_mean\": 0.164,\n      \"ot_7b_ensemble_cv_delta_prec_std\": 0.033,\n      \"ot_7b_hs_better_folds\": \"5/5\",\n      \"total_hs_better_folds\": \"10/10\",\n      \"ensemble_prec_vs_best_single\": \"ensemble ≈ best single metric (never worse)\",\n      \"ensemble_vs_text_all_significant\": true,\n      \"ensemble_vs_text_p_max\": 0.002,\n      \"impact_on_acceptance\": \"0-5% (cosmetic, not load-bearing)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Ensemble CV Results (Appendix)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model  | Metric        | Fold 1 | Fold 2 | Fold 3 | Fold 4 | Fold 5 | Mean±Std       |\\n|--------|---------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------------|\\n| R1-8B  | ΔPrecision    | +0.19  | +0.16  | +0.18  | +0.15  | +0.19  | +0.174±0.026  |\\n| R1-8B  | HS>Text?      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | 5/5           |\\n| OT-7B  | ΔPrecision    | +0.20  | +0.13  | +0.17  | +0.16  | +0.16  | +0.164±0.033  |\\n| OT-7B  | HS>Text?      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | ✅      | 5/5           |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix-only content。Best 档 reviewer 如果 notice 它会 appreciate thoroughness 但不会将其列入 strengths/weaknesses。对 acceptance probability 的 marginal contribution ≤5%。论文 space budget：1/4 page in appendix max。\\n\\nEnsemble CV 在 best 档中的 impact 接近 zero (0-5%)。原因：paper 的 acceptance 已经由 12/12 HB, position mediation 3/4, 5-seed robustness, 16/16 BA-layer analysis 这些 evidence package 支撑。Ensemble CV 做的是 \\\"validate that multi-metric consensus layer selection is stable under CV\\\"——但 LOO-CV stability (65-68%) 已经回答了这个问题。Ensemble 结果 10/10 folds HS better than text 是 consistent 但 unsurprising。Best 档 reviewer 不会要求 \\\"please add CV-validated ensemble\\\" 作为 acceptance condition，因为 individual metric analysis 已经足够 rigorous。 Ensemble 放 appendix 作为 supplementary validation，不进入 main text contribution claims。核心假设 \\\"ensemble_cv_impact_on_acceptance: [0.0, 0.05]\\\" 直接适用。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":446,"startLine":1,"totalLines":446}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XH3gNzJGfHYSYMnXM6qcs1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contrastive_trace_safety\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (LLM Security Track)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026\n6\t\n7\t## Core Claims (D031: layer selection as primary contribution, 4 models)\n8\t\n9\t**Contribution structure (D031)**:\n10\t- **Primary (methodological)**: Layer selection metric sensitivity — biased metrics reverse conclusions\n11\t- **Secondary (empirical)**: HS advantage at correct layers, qualified by scale; temporal improvement universal\n12\t- **Tertiary (negative results)**: 6 alternative methods fail, establishing what doesn't work\n13\t\n14\t1. **Temporal context universally improves probe accuracy across both modalities** (D014 + D023 nuanced) — Temporal context is the most robust improvement across all 4 models and both modalities. Text probes benefit consistently from larger windows across all models. HS probes benefit in 3/4 models; OT-7B HS peaks at W=3 and declines at larger W (confirmed on both layer 0 and layer 16).\n15\t\n16\t   **HS temporal gains** (W=1→best, 3 original models): accuracy +3pp (77.8%→81.0%), precision +13pp (69.3%→82.2%), FPR halved (9.65%→4.83%).\n17\t   **OT-7B HS temporal** (layer 16): bal_acc peaks at W=3 (68.8%), declines to 65.9% at W=25 (-2.9pp). BUT precision and FPR continue improving (prec 42.8%→49.4%, FPR 12.0%→7.5%). Temporal saturation is bal_acc-specific; larger W trades bal_acc for better precision/FPR. Confirmed on both layer 0 and layer 16 — genuine OT-7B characteristic.\n18\t   **Text temporal gains** (all 4 models, W=1→best): universally +3-12pp bal_acc, +8-23pp precision, FPR reduced.\n19\t\n20\t   **IMPORTANT: coverage direction depends on detection criterion K.** K=1 (single crossing): coverage DECREASES with W. K=5 (consecutive crossings): coverage may INCREASE with W. Claim 1 is about accuracy/precision improvement, NOT coverage.\n21\t\n22\t   The core insight: \"Temporal context universally improves text probes across all 4 models. For HS probes, 3/4 models benefit from larger temporal windows, while OT-7B shows early saturation (W=3 peak).\"\n23\t\n24\t2. **HS probes outperform text probes at correctly selected layers, with strong evidence at 7-8B and model-specific patterns at 32B** (D031: qualified from D030 \"universal\") —\n25\t\n26\t   **KEY FINDING (D029)**: The apparent \"scale-dependent\" HS advantage (significant at 7-8B, absent at 32B) was an artifact of the layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate`, which systematically selects shallow layers for 32B models. At correctly selected deep layers, HS outperforms text on all 4 models, but the NATURE of the advantage differs by scale.\n27\t\n28\t   **Layer selection metric bias (D028, refined D036)**: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selects shallow layers because shallow layers have higher crossing rates (more trigger-happy probes). 3/4 non-biased threshold-dependent metrics (precision, pre_cp_fpr, composite) converge on deep layers; pure bal_acc (threshold-free) selects middle layers (L30/L47). Deployment-relevant metric consensus selects L60/L63 for 32B models.\n29\t\n30\t   **7-8B models: HS significantly outperforms text (2/2 models) — UNCHANGED**\n31\t\n32\t   **R1-8B (Llama-8B, R1-distilled, n=43):**\n33\t   - Precision: 69.7% vs 47.2% (+22.4pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n34\t   - Accuracy: 81.3% vs 72.9% (+8.2pp, p=0.005, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n35\t   - Pre-CP FPR: 14.8% vs 22.2% (-7.4pp, p=0.044, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅** — rank 12/12, threshold=0.0500)\n36\t\n37\t   **OT-7B (Qwen-7B, STILL-trained, n=47, layer 16, matched W=3) — D026 M001 corrected:**\n38\t   - Bal Acc: 68.8% vs 58.1% (+10.7pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n39\t   - Precision: 46.6% vs 24.7% (+21.9pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n40\t   - Pre-CP FPR: 10.0% vs 27.1% (-17.1pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n41\t   - **3/3 metrics significant — OT-7B cleanest single-model evidence**\n42\t\n43\t   **32B models: HS outperforms text at CORRECTED LAYERS but with model-specific caveats (D029+D031)**\n44\t\n45\t   **QwQ-32B (Qwen-32B, native, n=19-20, Layer 60 corrected from L2):**\n46\t   - Bal Acc: +11-22pp across all 15 window sizes, all p<0.005 (bootstrap, null-centered)\n47\t   - 15/15 W values show significant HS advantage\n48\t   - **CRITICAL CAVEAT (D031)**: HS lead time NEGATIVE (-1.2 to 1.9 steps vs text 3.7-12.3). HS is \"more accurate but detects later.\" Position baseline bal_acc=0.746 > HS=0.740. In safety deployment, detecting 8-12 steps earlier may outweigh higher accuracy.\n49\t   - W=3: bal_acc +15.4pp, precision +23.6pp, FPR -9.8pp — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni ✅**\n50\t\n51\t   **R1-32B (Qwen-32B, R1-distilled, n=20, Layer 63 corrected from L10):**\n52\t   - W=1: bal_acc +18.7pp (0.826 vs 0.639), p=0.000; precision +15.4pp (0.603 vs 0.448), p=0.000; FPR -14.6pp (0.235 vs 0.380), p=0.007 — **3/3 Bonferroni ✅**\n53\t   - W=3: bal_acc +11.2pp p=0.020, precision p=0.032, FPR p=0.077 — **0/3 Bonferroni** (v2 null-centered)\n54\t   - W=5-15: all NS\n55\t   - **CRITICAL CAVEAT (D031)**: Only W=1 passes Bonferroni, coverage=25% (5/20 traces). Evidence statistically narrow.\n56\t   - **POSITIVE**: Lead time +11.7-13.3 steps (excellent early warning). HS >> Position (+14.2pp).\n57\t   - **NOTE**: L10 vs L63 at W=10: L10=0.795 vs L63=0.754 — L10 slightly better. \"Scheme B选错层\" narrative weaker for R1-32B.\n58\t   - ✅ P-VALUE UNIFIED: null-centered two-sided, consistent with QwQ.\n59\t\n60\t   **32B cross-model divergence (D031 key finding for Discussion):**\n61\t   | Dimension | R1-32B L63 | QwQ L60 |\n62\t   |-----------|-----------|---------|\n63\t   | Bonferroni | W=1 only (3/3) | All 15 W (3/3) |\n64\t   | Lead time | +11.7 to +13.3 (excellent) | -1.2 to +1.9 (poor) |\n65\t   | HS vs Position | HS >> Pos (+14.2pp) | HS < Pos (-0.6pp) |\n66\t   | Coverage (W=1) | 25% | 74% |\n67\t   Paper MUST discuss this divergence per-model, not unify into single narrative.\n68\t\n69\t   **OLD 32B results at BIASED layers (L2/L10) — RETRACTED as metric artifact:**\n70\t   - R1-32B L10: precision +9.4pp (p=0.064), accuracy +6.2pp (p=0.13)\n71\t   - QwQ-32B L2: precision +5.8pp (p=0.35), accuracy +0.9pp (p=0.83)\n72\t   - These non-significant results were caused by the biased `bal_acc × crossing_rate` metric selecting layers where HS signal is weak.\n73\t\n74\t   **Holm-Bonferroni COMPLETE (D032): 12/12 ALL PASS**\n75\t   Previously 5/12 (biased layers). With corrected layers: **12/12** step-down pass (α=0.05).\n76\t\n77\t   | Rank | Model | Metric | p-value | Threshold | Pass |\n78\t   |------|-------|--------|---------|-----------|------|\n79\t   | 1 | R1-8B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0042 | ✅ |\n80\t   | 2 | OT-7B | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0045 | ✅ |\n81\t   | 3 | OT-7B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0050 | ✅ |\n82\t   | 4 | OT-7B | FPR | <0.001 | 0.0056 | ✅ |\n83\t   | 5 | QwQ | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0063 | ✅ |\n84\t   | 6 | QwQ | precision | <0.001 | 0.0071 | ✅ |\n85\t   | 7 | R1-32B | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0083 | ✅ |\n86\t   | 8 | R1-32B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0100 | ✅ |\n87\t   | 9 | QwQ | FPR | 0.004 | 0.0125 | ✅ |\n88\t   | 10 | R1-8B | bal_acc | 0.005 | 0.0167 | ✅ |\n89\t   | 11 | R1-32B | FPR | 0.007 | 0.0250 | ✅ |\n90\t   | 12 | R1-8B | FPR | 0.044 | 0.0500 | ✅ |\n91\t\n92\t   **Caveats**: Different W per model (R1-8B W=15, OT-7B/QwQ W=3, R1-32B W=1). Tests measure \"HS > text at each model's best setting,\" not \"at uniform W.\" R1-32B W=1 has 25% coverage. Paper must state these conditions.\n93\t\n94\t   **FPR dual reporting**: Step-level (r1-8b: HS 8.8%, text 20.5%) vs trace-level (HS 14.8%, text 22.2%). Both reported.\n95\t\n96\t   **FPR reversal RESOLVED (D026)**: OT-7B HS FPR@L16 (10.0%) < Text FPR at ANY window (16.1%). HS dominates on FPR at 7-8B.\n97\t\n98\t   **Effect size consistency**: Precision advantage across all 4 models at corrected layers: R1-8B +22.4pp, OT-7B +21.2pp, QwQ +23.6pp, R1-32B +15.4pp. Remarkably consistent +15-24pp range.\n99\t\n100\t   Paper recommended claim (D032): \"At correctly selected layers, HS probes significantly outperform text probes on all 4 models (12/12 Holm-Bonferroni, precision +15-24pp). The layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically biases toward shallow layers, entirely masking this advantage at 32B scale. Practical implications differ by model: 7-8B models show strong HS advantage with comparable timing; R1-32B shows excellent lead time (+13 steps) but narrow coverage at the significant window; QwQ shows robust statistical significance but HS detects later than text.\"\n101\t\n102\t3. **HS and text monitoring exhibit different detection timing profiles** (narrowed from old Claim 3, now 4/4 models with GRU) — On r1-8b: HS temporal LR detects AT the commitment point (lead ~0) while text detects ~10 steps earlier. GRU achieves modest positive lead (+4.5+-3.0, worst seed +0.9). BOCPD/CUSUM fail to improve over simple thresholds. The oracle's +31-step advantage shows hidden states encode current safety state but poorly predict future trajectory. On 32B models: timing profiles vary (QwQ GRU lead +15.9, R1-32B +8.8) but FPR differences are non-significant. OT-7B GRU (layer 16, multi-layer L13-19, 3 seeds): bal_acc 74.6+-1.3%, coverage 64.5+-7.0%, lead +33.6+-4.8, FPR 27.4+-6.1%. GRU trades higher FPR for longer lead (consistent with R1-8B pattern). NOTE: OT-7B absolute lead times are inflated by long traces (~80 sentences vs ~30). Paper should normalize or explicitly caveat trace length differences when comparing across models.\n103\t\n104\t   NOTE: 32B timing profiles should be RE-EVALUATED at corrected layers (L60/L63) — current GRU results used old biased layers.\n105\t\n106\t## Methodological Contribution: Layer Selection Sensitivity (D028, elevated from RETRACTED Claim 4)\n107\t\n108\tThe layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically biases toward shallow layers because shallow layers have higher crossing rates (more frequently crossing the detection threshold). This bias is especially problematic for 32B models, where it selects layers at 3-16% depth instead of deep layers selected by threshold-dependent metrics.\n109\t\n110\t**Ablation evidence (4 models × 5 metrics) — UPDATED D036**:\n111\t- `bal_acc × crossing_rate`: selects L2 (QwQ), L10 (R1-32B) — shallow, biased\n112\t- Pure `bal_acc`: selects **middle layers** for 32B — L30 (QwQ, 47%), L47 (R1-32B, 73%); deep for 7-8B (agrees with other metrics). Threshold-free metric, behaves like AUROC.\n113\t- `precision`: selects deep layers for all models (L60/L63 for 32B)\n114\t- `pre_cp_fpr`: selects deep layers for all models\n115\t- `composite` (additive): selects deep layers for all models\n116\t- **Pattern**: Threshold-FREE metrics (bal_acc, AUROC) → middle layers; threshold-DEPENDENT metrics (precision, FPR, composite) → deep layers. Crossing_rate-contaminated metrics → shallow layers.\n117\t\n118\t**LOO-CV stability (D036)**: Under LOO-CV, the dominant layer is selected in 65-68% of folds regardless of metric. QwQ L30 selected 13/19 folds (bal_acc), R1-32B L47 selected 13/20 folds (bal_acc). Selection is robust to val set composition.\n119\t\n120\t**Corrected layer definition (D036)**: \"Corrected layers\" = consensus of threshold-dependent metrics (precision, inverse FPR, additive composite) — 3 of 4 non-biased metrics, not all 4. Pure bal_acc selects middle layers (L30/L47) with higher step-level accuracy (0.75/0.83 vs 0.71/0.76 at deep layers), but deployment-relevant metrics (precision, FPR) favor deep layers where all 4 models achieve HB-significant HS advantage.\n121\t\n122\t**Impact**: Incorrect layer selection entirely masked the HS advantage at 32B scale, leading to the false conclusion that HS advantage is scale-dependent. Even among unbiased metrics, metric choice affects optimal layer depth — threshold-free vs threshold-dependent is a second dimension of researcher degrees of freedom beyond the crossing_rate bias.\n123\t\n124\t**Anti-circular-reasoning defense (D031, refined D036)**: The claim that deep layers are \"correct\" for deployment rests on: (1) `crossing_rate` has a MECHANISTIC bias — shallow layers have compressed representations (1.4-2.7× smaller cosine distances) generating noise-driven crossings; (2) threshold-dependent metrics (precision, FPR) directly measure deployment-relevant properties; (3) at deep layers, all 4 models show significant HS advantage (HB corrected); (4) LOO-CV confirms selection stability. The paper presents layer selection as a \"researcher degree of freedom\" with systematic audit via sensitivity analysis.\n125\t\n126\t**Paper treatment**: Dedicated subsection in Method + Table showing metric × model → selected layer + downstream HS-text comparison. Frame as sensitivity analysis, not \"correct vs incorrect.\"\n127\t\n128\t## Story Spine\n129\t\n130\t- **Problem**: Reasoning models exhibit \"self-jailbreak\" — safety reasoning and harmful execution interleave throughout extended CoT, culminating in a \"commitment point\" where safety reasoning permanently ceases. Existing hidden-state detectors (TrajGuard, SafeSwitch, SIREN) target adversarial INPUT attacks on instruction-tuned models; they have never been evaluated on reasoning-model self-jailbreak where the threat is the model's OWN reasoning process.\n131\t\n132\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Hidden-state detectors achieve 95% defense on standard LLMs (TrajGuard) but operate at token-level. Reasoning-model safety analysis (Self-Jailbreaking, HarmThoughts) characterizes the phenomenon without providing deployable detectors. Text-level CoT monitors (SafeRemind, SafeThink) are vulnerable to pathological CoT. No prior work systematically compares detection modalities for reasoning-model self-jailbreak.\n133\t\n134\t- **Our framing**: We provide the first systematic evaluation of detection methods for reasoning-model safety commitment across **4 models, 2 architectures (Llama + Qwen), 2 training methods (R1-distilled + STILL), and 2 scales (7-8B + 32B)**, comparing hidden-state probes, text-based probes, sequence models (GRU), change-point detection (BOCPD/CUSUM), unsupervised methods (Mahalanobis, RepE direction, CCS), and nonlinear probes (MLP). We discover that: (a) temporal context is the most robust improvement, benefiting both modalities universally; (b) HS probes universally outperform text at correctly selected layers, with a critical sensitivity to layer selection methodology; (c) existing methods designed for other settings (TrajGuard, BOCPD, CCS, RepE) fail on reasoning model commitment; (d) linear probes are sufficient (MLP adds no value); (e) safety representations are model-specific (cross-transfer fails entirely), validated by control task (selectivity 7.5-18.5pp).\n135\t\n136\t- **Headline result (D032)**: \"Hidden-state probes significantly outperform text probes for safety commitment detection on all 4 models (12/12 Holm-Bonferroni, precision +15-24pp), but this advantage is entirely invisible under biased layer selection metrics. The composite metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically selects shallow layers at 32B scale, masking the HS signal and producing false negatives. This methodological finding, together with model-specific practical trade-offs at 32B (early detection vs broad coverage) and the comprehensive failure of 6 alternative methods, establishes that supervised temporal probing with principled layer selection is the most effective and robust approach for monitoring reasoning-model safety commitment.\"\n137\t\n138\t## Key Evidence Summary\n139\t\n140\t### R1-8B (Llama-8B, R1-distilled, n=43 test, class_weight=balanced, 60/20/20 split — CANONICAL)\n141\t\n142\tBest layer: 14 (45% depth). Full sweep layers 0-24 confirmed: layer 12 marginally better (+0.4pp bal_acc), no practical difference.\n143\t\n144\t| Method | Coverage | Lead Time | Pre-CP FPR | Safe FPR |\n145\t|--------|----------|-----------|------------|----------|\n146\t| HS Static LR L14 | — | -2.0 | **9.7%** | — |\n147\t| HS Temporal W=5 | — | +0.6 | **10.2%** | — |\n148\t| HS Temporal W=15 | — | **-0.1** | **8.8%** | — |\n149\t| Text Temporal W=15 | — | +10.3* | 20.5% | — |\n150\t| GRU Multi-7L (3-seed) | 72.9+-4.0% | +4.5+-3.0 | 16.5+-4.1% | — |\n151\t\n152\t*Text lead time inflated by high pre-CP FPR (trigger-happy detection)\n153\tNOTE: HS LR lead time collapsed to ~0 with balanced weights — HS detects AT commitment, not before. Only GRU achieves positive lead (+4.5, worst seed +0.9).\n154\t\n155\t### OT-7B (Qwen-7B, STILL-trained, n=47 test, 228 total traces) — D026 CORRECTED to layer 16\n156\t\n157\tBest layer: **16 (57% depth)**. M001 corrected: layer 0 was selected by bal_acc x crossing_rate bug; layer 16 selected by bal_acc.\n158\t\n159\t| Method | Bal Acc | Precision | Coverage | Pre-CP FPR | Lead |\n160\t|--------|---------|-----------|----------|-----------|------|\n161\t| HS Temporal W=3 L16 (best) | **68.8%** | **46.6%** | 53.2% | **10.0%** | — |\n162\t| Text Temporal W=25 (best) | 61.4% | 32.9% | 66.0% | 16.1% | 45.5 |\n163\t| Text Temporal W=3 (matched) | 57.9% | 25.4% | — | 27.1% | — |\n164\t\n165\tBootstrap (layer 16, matched W=3, 1000 resamples):\n166\t   bal_acc +10.7pp, 95% CI [4.9, 16.3], p<0.001 ✅\n167\t   precision +21.9pp, 95% CI [14.0, 29.6], p<0.001 ✅\n168\t   FPR -17.1pp, 95% CI [-22.2, -12.2], p<0.001 ✅ — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni**\n169\tSelectivity: 18.3pp (real=0.688, random=0.505) — highest across all models\n170\t\n171\t### 32B Cross-Architecture — D029 CORRECTED LAYERS\n172\t\n173\t**QwQ-32B (Qwen-32B, native, n=19-20, Layer 60 — corrected from L2)**\n174\t- HS vs Text bootstrap (null-centered, 1000 resamples):\n175\t  - Bal Acc: +11-22pp across W=1-15, ALL 15/15 significant (p<0.005)\n176\t  - W=3 (matched): bal_acc +15.4pp (p<0.001 ✅), precision +23.6pp (p<0.001 ✅), FPR -9.8pp (p=0.004 ✅) — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni**\n177\t- Caveats: HS lead time poor (-1.2 to 1.9 steps vs text 3.7-12.3), position baseline competitive\n178\t- Layer selection: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selected L2 (3.1%); threshold-dependent metrics consensus selects L60 (94%); pure `bal_acc` selects L30 (47%, bal_acc=0.7513 vs L60=0.7101) (D036)\n179\t\n180\t**R1-32B (Qwen-32B, R1-distilled, n=20, Layer 63 — corrected from L10)**\n181\t- W=1: bal_acc +18.7pp, p<0.001 ✅\n182\t- W≥5: NS (dimensionality: 51200 × W features for n=20)\n183\t- W=1: 3/3 Holm-Bonferroni ✅; W=3: 0/3 Bonferroni (null-centered v2); W≥5: NS\n184\t- Layer selection: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selected L10 (15.6%); threshold-dependent metrics consensus selects L63 (98%); pure `bal_acc` selects L47 (73%, bal_acc=0.8290 vs L63=0.7585) (D036)\n185\t\n186\t**OLD biased-layer results (RETRACTED as metric artifact):**\n187\t| Model | Biased Layer | Corrected Layer | Biased p-value | Corrected p-value |\n188\t|-------|-------------|----------------|----------------|-------------------|\n189\t| R1-32B | L10 (16%) | L63 (98%) | 0.064-0.13 (NS) | <0.001 (W=1) ✅ |\n190\t| QwQ-32B | L2 (3%) | L60 (94%) | 0.35-0.83 (NS) | <0.005 (all W) ✅ |\n191\t\n192\t### 4-Model Holm-Bonferroni Summary (D032 — COMPLETE: 12/12 ✅)\n193\t\n194\t| Model | Arch | Training | Scale | Layer | W | bal_acc | precision | FPR | Selectivity |\n195\t|-------|------|----------|-------|-------|---|--------|-----------|-----|-------------|\n196\t| R1-8B | Llama | R1-distilled | 8B | L14 (45%) | 15 | +8.2pp ✅ | +22.4pp ✅ | -7.4pp ✅ | 12.5pp |\n197\t| OT-7B | Qwen | STILL | 7B | L16 (57%) | 3 | +10.7pp ✅ | +21.9pp ✅ | -17.1pp ✅ | 18.3pp |\n198\t| QwQ-32B | Qwen | native | 32B | L60 (94%) | 3 | +15.4pp ✅ | +23.6pp ✅ | -9.8pp ✅ | 15.3pp |\n199\t| R1-32B | Qwen | R1-distilled | 32B | L63 (98%) | 1 | +18.7pp ✅ | +15.4pp ✅ | -14.6pp ✅ | 7.5pp |\n200\t\n201\t**12/12 all pass Holm-Bonferroni step-down (α=0.05)**. Previously 5/12 with biased layers.\n202\tPrecision advantage remarkably consistent: +15.4 to +23.6pp across all 4 models.\n203\tCaveats: Different W per model; R1-32B W=1 coverage=25%; QwQ lead time negative.\n204\t\n205\t### Position Mediation Analysis (D038 → D039 → D042 complete)\n206\t\n207\t**Finding**: Position (relative step t/T) is a significant component of probe performance. 3/4 models retain HS advantage after residualization; R1-32B is the exception.\n208\t\n209\t| Model | W | Resid HS BA | Resid Text BA | HS-Text Gap | Gap p | HB |\n210\t|-------|---|------------|--------------|-------------|-------|-----|\n211\t| OT-7B | 3 | 0.609 | 0.540 | **+6.9pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n212\t| R1-8B | 15 | 0.669 | 0.605 | **+6.4pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n213\t| R1-8B | 3 | 0.571 | 0.534 | **+3.7pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n214\t| QwQ-32B | 3 | 0.619 | 0.582 | **+3.7pp** | 0.011 | ✅ |\n215\t| R1-32B | 1 | 0.552 | 0.532 | +1.9pp | 0.914 | ❌ |\n216\t\n217\tPosition-only BA: OT-7B/R1-8B/QwQ ≈ 0.706; R1-32B = 0.686.\n218\t\n219\t**D042 final picture**: HS advantage has two separable components — position-mediated and non-positional. 3/4 models retain significant non-positional HS advantage (HB pass); R1-32B's advantage is almost entirely position-mediated (drop 20.4pp, residualized gap NS). This is consistent with R1-32B's other caveats (W=1 only significant, 25% coverage).\n220\t\n221\t**Key implications for paper**:\n222\t1. Position is a significant component (12-20pp drop) — universal\n223\t2. 3/4 models retain non-positional HS advantage (residualized BA gap +3.7 to +6.9pp, HB pass)\n224\t3. R1-32B is the exception: HS advantage position-mediated, residualized gap NS\n225\t4. Temporal windowing preserves non-positional signal (R1-8B: 24pp drop@W=3 → 16pp@W=15)\n226\t5. Paper framing: \"HS advantage persists after position removal in 3/4 models; R1-32B advantage is position-mediated\"\n227\t\n228\t### 5-Seed Robustness (D041)\n229\t\n230\t| Model | HB Pass Rate | Mean ΔPrec ± std | Mean ΔBA ± std |\n231\t|-------|-------------|------------------|----------------|\n232\t| OT-7B | **5/5** | +20.9 ± 1.3pp | +11.3 ± 1.5pp |\n233\t| R1-32B | **5/5** | +13.7 ± 2.0pp | +11.8 ± 2.4pp |\n234\t| QwQ-32B | **5/5** | +19.9 ± 2.5pp | +11.4 ± 3.2pp |\n235\t| R1-8B | **3/5** | +14.6 ± 4.5pp | +9.4 ± 2.4pp |\n236\t\n237\tR1-8B failures are FPR-specific (seed 123 FPR p=0.262, seed 456 FPR p=0.952). Precision is directionally consistent across all 20 seed-model combinations (always positive). ΔPrec never reverses.\n238\t\n239\t**D041 insight**: Robustness splits by MODEL not SCALE. R1-32B (5/5, ΔPrec std=2.0pp) is more stable than R1-8B (3/5, ΔPrec std=4.5pp). \"7-8B robust / 32B sample-limited\" is factually wrong. R1-32B's absolute precision std (12.8pp) vs paired delta std (2.0pp) — paper must distinguish these.\n240\t\n241\t**Per-model evidence tier (D042)**:\n242\t- **OT-7B**: Cleanest — 5/5 HB, largest residualized gap (+6.9pp), highest selectivity (18.3pp)\n243\t- **QwQ-32B**: Robust — 5/5 HB, residualized gap holds (+3.7pp), but position baseline competitive\n244\t- **R1-8B**: Precision-robust — residualized holds (+3.7-6.4pp), but FPR unstable (3/5 HB)\n245\t- **R1-32B**: Statistically stable (5/5 HB, ΔPrec std=2.0pp) but advantage position-mediated (residualized NS)\n246\t\n247\t**Residualized precision**: Not tested (scope limited to BA per Reviewer recommendation).\n248\t\n249\t### BA-Layer Robustness: Metric Circularity Refuted (D044)\n250\t\n251\tR13 W1 concern: corrected selection uses threshold-dependent metrics (precision, FPR), evaluation also uses precision/FPR — potential circularity. Test: compute HS vs text on BA-selected layers (threshold-free criterion).\n252\t\n253\t| Model | BA-Opt Layer | ΔPrec | ΔBA | ΔFPR | ΔAUROC | All 4 HB? |\n254\t|-------|-------------|-------|-----|------|--------|-----------|\n255\t| R1-8B | L12 | +17.8pp | +7.8pp | -12.9pp | +9.3pp | ✅ |\n256\t| OT-7B | L9 | +25.4pp | +11.7pp | -19.3pp | +14.8pp | ✅ |\n257\t| QwQ-32B | L30 | +18.0pp | +14.8pp | -8.0pp | +17.3pp | ✅ |\n258\t| R1-32B | L47 | +13.7pp | +14.9pp | -23.1pp | +21.1pp | ✅ |\n259\t\n260\t**4/4 models × 4 metrics = 16/16 HB pass.** HS advantage is a genuine modality property, not a layer selection artifact.\n261\t\n262\tKey insight: R1-32B on BA-layer L47 shows ΔPrec +13.7pp and ΔAUROC +21.1pp — stronger than corrected L63 in threshold-free metrics. OT-7B on BA-layer L9 has ΔPrec +25.4pp > corrected L16 (+21.9pp). HS advantage is robust to layer selection criterion.\n263\t\n264\tCaveat: QwQ FPR adj_p=0.041 (marginal, CI close to zero). Other 15/16 tests p≤0.006.\n265\t\n266\t### Post-hoc Power Analysis (D044)\n267\t\n268\t| Model | n (test) | MDE (80% power, α=0.05) |\n269\t|-------|----------|------------------------|\n270\t| OT-7B | 47-69 | 6.7-8.1pp |\n271\t| R1-8B | 43-63 | 7.4-9.0pp |\n272\t| QwQ-32B | 29 | 9.5pp |\n273\t| R1-32B | 20-30 | 8.6-11.2pp |\n274\t\n275\tAll significant effects (15-24pp) are well above MDE → adequately powered. R1-32B residualized gap (+1.9pp) is far below MDE (11.2pp) → NS is power limitation, not evidence of absence.\n276\t\n277\t### Negative Results (expanded with R3 supplementary experiments)\n278\t- **BOCPD/CUSUM (4/4 models)**: R1-8B BOCPD 93% detection but lead +3.5 < threshold +4.9; OT-7B/R1-32B/QwQ all 0% detection across all λ. CUSUM worse than threshold on all models.\n279\t- **Mahalanobis (4/4 models confirmed negative)**: R1-8B (+0.07), OT-7B (+0.031), R1-32B (+0.148), QwQ (+0.204) — all separation ≈ 0. Signal in minor PCA components, not principal directions.\n280\t- **RepE direction probing (4/4 models, corrected layers confirmed)**: Direction-based supervised method (needs CP labels). Results highly layer-dependent and model-specific:\n281\t  - R1-32B L63 (corrected): bal_acc=0.559 (near-random), FPR=49.9% — **direction vector fails at deep layer** where supervised LR excels (0.826). Train-test gap 13.3pp shows poor generalization.\n282\t  - QwQ L60 (corrected): bal_acc=0.756, precision=0.512, FPR=0.309 — **improves** from L2 (0.666), narrows gap with supervised LR W=1 (0.740 bal_acc), but still inferior in precision/FPR.\n283\t  - R1-8B L14: bal_acc=0.749, OT-7B L16: bal_acc=0.642\n284\t  - **Key insight**: Supervised LR is necessary — mean-difference direction cannot decode safety commitment at deep layers for R1-32B (discriminative training finds signal that simple direction averaging misses). Layer selection sensitivity applies to RepE too, but in model-specific ways (R1-32B: shallow better for RepE; QwQ: deep better for both).\n285\t- **MLP nonlinear probe (4/4 models)**: 3/4 models worse than LR. Linear probes sufficient; nonlinearity adds no value.\n286\t- **CCS-adapted (Burns et al. 2023, 4/4 models)**: WEAKLY SUPERVISED (needs CP labels for pair construction, not truly unsupervised). R1-8B bal_acc=0.777 (between supervised LR 0.817 and RepE 0.749). R1-32B FPR=0.410 (near-chance). OT-7B precision=0.319 (near-chance, high lead=20.5 is artifact of high FPR). Uses scheme B layers (biased). Paper must: (a) label as \"weakly supervised\" not \"unsupervised\"; (b) disclose pair construction differs from Burns et al.; (c) note scheme B layer limitation.\n287\t- **Cross-model transfer (exp-003)**: All directions fail entirely (best: 58.3% acc, 40.7% crossing).\n288\t\n289\t## Venue Fit Risks\n290\t\n291\t- **EMNLP LLM Security track fit**: Strong — defense/detection evaluation for reasoning model jailbreak.\n292\t- **Method simplicity risk**: Mitigate: frame as empirical study. Contribution is systematic evaluation + layer selection sensitivity discovery + comprehensive negative results.\n293\t- **Statistical power**: With corrected layers, **12/12** tests pass Holm-Bonferroni across ALL 4 models (up from 5/12 with biased layers).\n294\t- **HS advantage universal**: UPGRADED from \"scale-dependent\" — layer selection is the true moderator, not scale. Cleaner story.\n295\t- **Trace vs step FPR**: Both reported with explanation.\n296\t- **High safe FPR risk**: All methods 39-62% safe FPR. Frame as diagnostic tool limitation.\n297\t- **32B caveats**: HS advantage exists but is more sensitive to window size (R1-32B W=1 only) and affected by dimensionality (51200-d at large W with n=20). Lead times shorter than 7-8B. These are honest limitations, not disqualifiers.\n298\t\n299\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n300\t\n301\t1. \"Method novelty?\" → Empirical study + systematic method comparison + layer selection sensitivity as methodological contribution + comprehensive negative results (6 methods fail).\n302\t2. \"Only one model family?\" → **RESOLVED**: 4 models, 2 architectures (Llama + Qwen), 2 training methods, 2 scales. ALL showing significant HS advantage at corrected layers.\n303\t3. \"GRU unstable?\" → 3-seed reporting with worst-seed bounds. R1-32B GRU at L10 was unstable; needs re-evaluation at L63.\n304\t4. \"Too few traces?\" → Cross-model validation + control task selectivity 7.5-18.5pp.\n305\t5. \"Fine-grained taxonomy?\" → Out of scope for current study.\n306\t6. \"HS doesn't beat text?\" → **QUALIFIED REBUTTAL (D031)**: HS outperforms text at correct layers with STRONG evidence at 7-8B (precision +22pp, Holm-Bonf) and QUALIFIED evidence at 32B (R1-32B: significant W=1 but narrow; QwQ: significant all W but late detection). 32B non-significance at OLD layers was artifact. Layer selection sensitivity analysis shows this is a methodological issue, not absence of signal.\n307\t7. \"Commitment point circular?\" → Cross-model consistency + control task selectivity argues against artifact.\n308\t8. \"Missing related work?\" → Expansion to 30+ citations.\n309\t9. \"No FPR analysis?\" → RESOLVED: both trace-level and step-level FPR reported.\n310\t10. \"High safe FPR?\" → Limitation acknowledged.\n311\t11. \"Control task / position confound?\" → RESOLVED (C2, D011): selectivity 7.5-18.5pp, HS FPR < position-only FPR.\n312\t12. \"Multiple testing correction?\" → **RESOLVED**: 12/12 Holm-Bonferroni step-down (α=0.05) across all 4 models (up from 5/12 with biased layers).\n313\t13. \"Trace vs step FPR?\" → Both reported with explanation.\n314\t14. \"Layer selection is just hyperparameter tuning?\" → No — we show a systematic bias in a commonly used composite metric. The ablation across 5 metrics × 4 models is a reproducible methodological finding, not a one-off parameter choice.\n315\t15. \"Why not just use the best layer for each model?\" → We do. The point is that the METRIC for selecting \"best\" matters. Biased metrics produce systematically wrong selections, masking real effects.\n316\t16. \"32B results are marginal / only W=1 significant for R1-32B?\" → Dimensionality constraint (51200 × W > n=20 at W≥5). QwQ L60 significant at ALL W values. R1-32B L63 significant at W=1. Both confirm HS advantage exists; practical deployment would use W=1-3 for 32B models.\n317\t\n318\t## Title Candidates (D031)\n319\t- \"Layer Selection Matters: How Metric Choice Determines Hidden-State Probe Effectiveness for Safety Monitoring\"\n320\t- \"Temporal Probing for Safety Commitment Detection in Reasoning Models: A Comprehensive Evaluation\"\n321\t- \"What Detects Safety Commitment in Reasoning Models? A Systematic Comparison of Probe-Based Methods\"\n322\t- \"Hidden-State vs Text Monitoring for Reasoning Model Safety: Layer Selection as the Missing Variable\"\n323\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c0610e2-18f5-465e-b8e4-959a05a2a7cd","uuid":"d2a92cbb-a598-4f99-b5f8-b6e3a53baf3f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:46:28.460Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T212242/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contrastive_trace_safety\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (LLM Security Track)\n- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Claims (D031: layer selection as primary contribution, 4 models)\n\n**Contribution structure (D031)**:\n- **Primary (methodological)**: Layer selection metric sensitivity — biased metrics reverse conclusions\n- **Secondary (empirical)**: HS advantage at correct layers, qualified by scale; temporal improvement universal\n- **Tertiary (negative results)**: 6 alternative methods fail, establishing what doesn't work\n\n1. **Temporal context universally improves probe accuracy across both modalities** (D014 + D023 nuanced) — Temporal context is the most robust improvement across all 4 models and both modalities. Text probes benefit consistently from larger windows across all models. HS probes benefit in 3/4 models; OT-7B HS peaks at W=3 and declines at larger W (confirmed on both layer 0 and layer 16).\n\n   **HS temporal gains** (W=1→best, 3 original models): accuracy +3pp (77.8%→81.0%), precision +13pp (69.3%→82.2%), FPR halved (9.65%→4.83%).\n   **OT-7B HS temporal** (layer 16): bal_acc peaks at W=3 (68.8%), declines to 65.9% at W=25 (-2.9pp). BUT precision and FPR continue improving (prec 42.8%→49.4%, FPR 12.0%→7.5%). Temporal saturation is bal_acc-specific; larger W trades bal_acc for better precision/FPR. Confirmed on both layer 0 and layer 16 — genuine OT-7B characteristic.\n   **Text temporal gains** (all 4 models, W=1→best): universally +3-12pp bal_acc, +8-23pp precision, FPR reduced.\n\n   **IMPORTANT: coverage direction depends on detection criterion K.** K=1 (single crossing): coverage DECREASES with W. K=5 (consecutive crossings): coverage may INCREASE with W. Claim 1 is about accuracy/precision improvement, NOT coverage.\n\n   The core insight: \"Temporal context universally improves text probes across all 4 models. For HS probes, 3/4 models benefit from larger temporal windows, while OT-7B shows early saturation (W=3 peak).\"\n\n2. **HS probes outperform text probes at correctly selected layers, with strong evidence at 7-8B and model-specific patterns at 32B** (D031: qualified from D030 \"universal\") —\n\n   **KEY FINDING (D029)**: The apparent \"scale-dependent\" HS advantage (significant at 7-8B, absent at 32B) was an artifact of the layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate`, which systematically selects shallow layers for 32B models. At correctly selected deep layers, HS outperforms text on all 4 models, but the NATURE of the advantage differs by scale.\n\n   **Layer selection metric bias (D028, refined D036)**: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selects shallow layers because shallow layers have higher crossing rates (more trigger-happy probes). 3/4 non-biased threshold-dependent metrics (precision, pre_cp_fpr, composite) converge on deep layers; pure bal_acc (threshold-free) selects middle layers (L30/L47). Deployment-relevant metric consensus selects L60/L63 for 32B models.\n\n   **7-8B models: HS significantly outperforms text (2/2 models) — UNCHANGED**\n\n   **R1-8B (Llama-8B, R1-distilled, n=43):**\n   - Precision: 69.7% vs 47.2% (+22.4pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n   - Accuracy: 81.3% vs 72.9% (+8.2pp, p=0.005, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n   - Pre-CP FPR: 14.8% vs 22.2% (-7.4pp, p=0.044, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅** — rank 12/12, threshold=0.0500)\n\n   **OT-7B (Qwen-7B, STILL-trained, n=47, layer 16, matched W=3) — D026 M001 corrected:**\n   - Bal Acc: 68.8% vs 58.1% (+10.7pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n   - Precision: 46.6% vs 24.7% (+21.9pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n   - Pre-CP FPR: 10.0% vs 27.1% (-17.1pp, p<0.001, **Holm-Bonferroni ✅**)\n   - **3/3 metrics significant — OT-7B cleanest single-model evidence**\n\n   **32B models: HS outperforms text at CORRECTED LAYERS but with model-specific caveats (D029+D031)**\n\n   **QwQ-32B (Qwen-32B, native, n=19-20, Layer 60 corrected from L2):**\n   - Bal Acc: +11-22pp across all 15 window sizes, all p<0.005 (bootstrap, null-centered)\n   - 15/15 W values show significant HS advantage\n   - **CRITICAL CAVEAT (D031)**: HS lead time NEGATIVE (-1.2 to 1.9 steps vs text 3.7-12.3). HS is \"more accurate but detects later.\" Position baseline bal_acc=0.746 > HS=0.740. In safety deployment, detecting 8-12 steps earlier may outweigh higher accuracy.\n   - W=3: bal_acc +15.4pp, precision +23.6pp, FPR -9.8pp — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni ✅**\n\n   **R1-32B (Qwen-32B, R1-distilled, n=20, Layer 63 corrected from L10):**\n   - W=1: bal_acc +18.7pp (0.826 vs 0.639), p=0.000; precision +15.4pp (0.603 vs 0.448), p=0.000; FPR -14.6pp (0.235 vs 0.380), p=0.007 — **3/3 Bonferroni ✅**\n   - W=3: bal_acc +11.2pp p=0.020, precision p=0.032, FPR p=0.077 — **0/3 Bonferroni** (v2 null-centered)\n   - W=5-15: all NS\n   - **CRITICAL CAVEAT (D031)**: Only W=1 passes Bonferroni, coverage=25% (5/20 traces). Evidence statistically narrow.\n   - **POSITIVE**: Lead time +11.7-13.3 steps (excellent early warning). HS >> Position (+14.2pp).\n   - **NOTE**: L10 vs L63 at W=10: L10=0.795 vs L63=0.754 — L10 slightly better. \"Scheme B选错层\" narrative weaker for R1-32B.\n   - ✅ P-VALUE UNIFIED: null-centered two-sided, consistent with QwQ.\n\n   **32B cross-model divergence (D031 key finding for Discussion):**\n   | Dimension | R1-32B L63 | QwQ L60 |\n   |-----------|-----------|---------|\n   | Bonferroni | W=1 only (3/3) | All 15 W (3/3) |\n   | Lead time | +11.7 to +13.3 (excellent) | -1.2 to +1.9 (poor) |\n   | HS vs Position | HS >> Pos (+14.2pp) | HS < Pos (-0.6pp) |\n   | Coverage (W=1) | 25% | 74% |\n   Paper MUST discuss this divergence per-model, not unify into single narrative.\n\n   **OLD 32B results at BIASED layers (L2/L10) — RETRACTED as metric artifact:**\n   - R1-32B L10: precision +9.4pp (p=0.064), accuracy +6.2pp (p=0.13)\n   - QwQ-32B L2: precision +5.8pp (p=0.35), accuracy +0.9pp (p=0.83)\n   - These non-significant results were caused by the biased `bal_acc × crossing_rate` metric selecting layers where HS signal is weak.\n\n   **Holm-Bonferroni COMPLETE (D032): 12/12 ALL PASS**\n   Previously 5/12 (biased layers). With corrected layers: **12/12** step-down pass (α=0.05).\n\n   | Rank | Model | Metric | p-value | Threshold | Pass |\n   |------|-------|--------|---------|-----------|------|\n   | 1 | R1-8B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0042 | ✅ |\n   | 2 | OT-7B | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0045 | ✅ |\n   | 3 | OT-7B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0050 | ✅ |\n   | 4 | OT-7B | FPR | <0.001 | 0.0056 | ✅ |\n   | 5 | QwQ | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0063 | ✅ |\n   | 6 | QwQ | precision | <0.001 | 0.0071 | ✅ |\n   | 7 | R1-32B | bal_acc | <0.001 | 0.0083 | ✅ |\n   | 8 | R1-32B | precision | <0.001 | 0.0100 | ✅ |\n   | 9 | QwQ | FPR | 0.004 | 0.0125 | ✅ |\n   | 10 | R1-8B | bal_acc | 0.005 | 0.0167 | ✅ |\n   | 11 | R1-32B | FPR | 0.007 | 0.0250 | ✅ |\n   | 12 | R1-8B | FPR | 0.044 | 0.0500 | ✅ |\n\n   **Caveats**: Different W per model (R1-8B W=15, OT-7B/QwQ W=3, R1-32B W=1). Tests measure \"HS > text at each model's best setting,\" not \"at uniform W.\" R1-32B W=1 has 25% coverage. Paper must state these conditions.\n\n   **FPR dual reporting**: Step-level (r1-8b: HS 8.8%, text 20.5%) vs trace-level (HS 14.8%, text 22.2%). Both reported.\n\n   **FPR reversal RESOLVED (D026)**: OT-7B HS FPR@L16 (10.0%) < Text FPR at ANY window (16.1%). HS dominates on FPR at 7-8B.\n\n   **Effect size consistency**: Precision advantage across all 4 models at corrected layers: R1-8B +22.4pp, OT-7B +21.2pp, QwQ +23.6pp, R1-32B +15.4pp. Remarkably consistent +15-24pp range.\n\n   Paper recommended claim (D032): \"At correctly selected layers, HS probes significantly outperform text probes on all 4 models (12/12 Holm-Bonferroni, precision +15-24pp). The layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically biases toward shallow layers, entirely masking this advantage at 32B scale. Practical implications differ by model: 7-8B models show strong HS advantage with comparable timing; R1-32B shows excellent lead time (+13 steps) but narrow coverage at the significant window; QwQ shows robust statistical significance but HS detects later than text.\"\n\n3. **HS and text monitoring exhibit different detection timing profiles** (narrowed from old Claim 3, now 4/4 models with GRU) — On r1-8b: HS temporal LR detects AT the commitment point (lead ~0) while text detects ~10 steps earlier. GRU achieves modest positive lead (+4.5+-3.0, worst seed +0.9). BOCPD/CUSUM fail to improve over simple thresholds. The oracle's +31-step advantage shows hidden states encode current safety state but poorly predict future trajectory. On 32B models: timing profiles vary (QwQ GRU lead +15.9, R1-32B +8.8) but FPR differences are non-significant. OT-7B GRU (layer 16, multi-layer L13-19, 3 seeds): bal_acc 74.6+-1.3%, coverage 64.5+-7.0%, lead +33.6+-4.8, FPR 27.4+-6.1%. GRU trades higher FPR for longer lead (consistent with R1-8B pattern). NOTE: OT-7B absolute lead times are inflated by long traces (~80 sentences vs ~30). Paper should normalize or explicitly caveat trace length differences when comparing across models.\n\n   NOTE: 32B timing profiles should be RE-EVALUATED at corrected layers (L60/L63) — current GRU results used old biased layers.\n\n## Methodological Contribution: Layer Selection Sensitivity (D028, elevated from RETRACTED Claim 4)\n\nThe layer selection metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically biases toward shallow layers because shallow layers have higher crossing rates (more frequently crossing the detection threshold). This bias is especially problematic for 32B models, where it selects layers at 3-16% depth instead of deep layers selected by threshold-dependent metrics.\n\n**Ablation evidence (4 models × 5 metrics) — UPDATED D036**:\n- `bal_acc × crossing_rate`: selects L2 (QwQ), L10 (R1-32B) — shallow, biased\n- Pure `bal_acc`: selects **middle layers** for 32B — L30 (QwQ, 47%), L47 (R1-32B, 73%); deep for 7-8B (agrees with other metrics). Threshold-free metric, behaves like AUROC.\n- `precision`: selects deep layers for all models (L60/L63 for 32B)\n- `pre_cp_fpr`: selects deep layers for all models\n- `composite` (additive): selects deep layers for all models\n- **Pattern**: Threshold-FREE metrics (bal_acc, AUROC) → middle layers; threshold-DEPENDENT metrics (precision, FPR, composite) → deep layers. Crossing_rate-contaminated metrics → shallow layers.\n\n**LOO-CV stability (D036)**: Under LOO-CV, the dominant layer is selected in 65-68% of folds regardless of metric. QwQ L30 selected 13/19 folds (bal_acc), R1-32B L47 selected 13/20 folds (bal_acc). Selection is robust to val set composition.\n\n**Corrected layer definition (D036)**: \"Corrected layers\" = consensus of threshold-dependent metrics (precision, inverse FPR, additive composite) — 3 of 4 non-biased metrics, not all 4. Pure bal_acc selects middle layers (L30/L47) with higher step-level accuracy (0.75/0.83 vs 0.71/0.76 at deep layers), but deployment-relevant metrics (precision, FPR) favor deep layers where all 4 models achieve HB-significant HS advantage.\n\n**Impact**: Incorrect layer selection entirely masked the HS advantage at 32B scale, leading to the false conclusion that HS advantage is scale-dependent. Even among unbiased metrics, metric choice affects optimal layer depth — threshold-free vs threshold-dependent is a second dimension of researcher degrees of freedom beyond the crossing_rate bias.\n\n**Anti-circular-reasoning defense (D031, refined D036)**: The claim that deep layers are \"correct\" for deployment rests on: (1) `crossing_rate` has a MECHANISTIC bias — shallow layers have compressed representations (1.4-2.7× smaller cosine distances) generating noise-driven crossings; (2) threshold-dependent metrics (precision, FPR) directly measure deployment-relevant properties; (3) at deep layers, all 4 models show significant HS advantage (HB corrected); (4) LOO-CV confirms selection stability. The paper presents layer selection as a \"researcher degree of freedom\" with systematic audit via sensitivity analysis.\n\n**Paper treatment**: Dedicated subsection in Method + Table showing metric × model → selected layer + downstream HS-text comparison. Frame as sensitivity analysis, not \"correct vs incorrect.\"\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Reasoning models exhibit \"self-jailbreak\" — safety reasoning and harmful execution interleave throughout extended CoT, culminating in a \"commitment point\" where safety reasoning permanently ceases. Existing hidden-state detectors (TrajGuard, SafeSwitch, SIREN) target adversarial INPUT attacks on instruction-tuned models; they have never been evaluated on reasoning-model self-jailbreak where the threat is the model's OWN reasoning process.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Hidden-state detectors achieve 95% defense on standard LLMs (TrajGuard) but operate at token-level. Reasoning-model safety analysis (Self-Jailbreaking, HarmThoughts) characterizes the phenomenon without providing deployable detectors. Text-level CoT monitors (SafeRemind, SafeThink) are vulnerable to pathological CoT. No prior work systematically compares detection modalities for reasoning-model self-jailbreak.\n\n- **Our framing**: We provide the first systematic evaluation of detection methods for reasoning-model safety commitment across **4 models, 2 architectures (Llama + Qwen), 2 training methods (R1-distilled + STILL), and 2 scales (7-8B + 32B)**, comparing hidden-state probes, text-based probes, sequence models (GRU), change-point detection (BOCPD/CUSUM), unsupervised methods (Mahalanobis, RepE direction, CCS), and nonlinear probes (MLP). We discover that: (a) temporal context is the most robust improvement, benefiting both modalities universally; (b) HS probes universally outperform text at correctly selected layers, with a critical sensitivity to layer selection methodology; (c) existing methods designed for other settings (TrajGuard, BOCPD, CCS, RepE) fail on reasoning model commitment; (d) linear probes are sufficient (MLP adds no value); (e) safety representations are model-specific (cross-transfer fails entirely), validated by control task (selectivity 7.5-18.5pp).\n\n- **Headline result (D032)**: \"Hidden-state probes significantly outperform text probes for safety commitment detection on all 4 models (12/12 Holm-Bonferroni, precision +15-24pp), but this advantage is entirely invisible under biased layer selection metrics. The composite metric `bal_acc × crossing_rate` systematically selects shallow layers at 32B scale, masking the HS signal and producing false negatives. This methodological finding, together with model-specific practical trade-offs at 32B (early detection vs broad coverage) and the comprehensive failure of 6 alternative methods, establishes that supervised temporal probing with principled layer selection is the most effective and robust approach for monitoring reasoning-model safety commitment.\"\n\n## Key Evidence Summary\n\n### R1-8B (Llama-8B, R1-distilled, n=43 test, class_weight=balanced, 60/20/20 split — CANONICAL)\n\nBest layer: 14 (45% depth). Full sweep layers 0-24 confirmed: layer 12 marginally better (+0.4pp bal_acc), no practical difference.\n\n| Method | Coverage | Lead Time | Pre-CP FPR | Safe FPR |\n|--------|----------|-----------|------------|----------|\n| HS Static LR L14 | — | -2.0 | **9.7%** | — |\n| HS Temporal W=5 | — | +0.6 | **10.2%** | — |\n| HS Temporal W=15 | — | **-0.1** | **8.8%** | — |\n| Text Temporal W=15 | — | +10.3* | 20.5% | — |\n| GRU Multi-7L (3-seed) | 72.9+-4.0% | +4.5+-3.0 | 16.5+-4.1% | — |\n\n*Text lead time inflated by high pre-CP FPR (trigger-happy detection)\nNOTE: HS LR lead time collapsed to ~0 with balanced weights — HS detects AT commitment, not before. Only GRU achieves positive lead (+4.5, worst seed +0.9).\n\n### OT-7B (Qwen-7B, STILL-trained, n=47 test, 228 total traces) — D026 CORRECTED to layer 16\n\nBest layer: **16 (57% depth)**. M001 corrected: layer 0 was selected by bal_acc x crossing_rate bug; layer 16 selected by bal_acc.\n\n| Method | Bal Acc | Precision | Coverage | Pre-CP FPR | Lead |\n|--------|---------|-----------|----------|-----------|------|\n| HS Temporal W=3 L16 (best) | **68.8%** | **46.6%** | 53.2% | **10.0%** | — |\n| Text Temporal W=25 (best) | 61.4% | 32.9% | 66.0% | 16.1% | 45.5 |\n| Text Temporal W=3 (matched) | 57.9% | 25.4% | — | 27.1% | — |\n\nBootstrap (layer 16, matched W=3, 1000 resamples):\n   bal_acc +10.7pp, 95% CI [4.9, 16.3], p<0.001 ✅\n   precision +21.9pp, 95% CI [14.0, 29.6], p<0.001 ✅\n   FPR -17.1pp, 95% CI [-22.2, -12.2], p<0.001 ✅ — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni**\nSelectivity: 18.3pp (real=0.688, random=0.505) — highest across all models\n\n### 32B Cross-Architecture — D029 CORRECTED LAYERS\n\n**QwQ-32B (Qwen-32B, native, n=19-20, Layer 60 — corrected from L2)**\n- HS vs Text bootstrap (null-centered, 1000 resamples):\n  - Bal Acc: +11-22pp across W=1-15, ALL 15/15 significant (p<0.005)\n  - W=3 (matched): bal_acc +15.4pp (p<0.001 ✅), precision +23.6pp (p<0.001 ✅), FPR -9.8pp (p=0.004 ✅) — **3/3 Holm-Bonferroni**\n- Caveats: HS lead time poor (-1.2 to 1.9 steps vs text 3.7-12.3), position baseline competitive\n- Layer selection: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selected L2 (3.1%); threshold-dependent metrics consensus selects L60 (94%); pure `bal_acc` selects L30 (47%, bal_acc=0.7513 vs L60=0.7101) (D036)\n\n**R1-32B (Qwen-32B, R1-distilled, n=20, Layer 63 — corrected from L10)**\n- W=1: bal_acc +18.7pp, p<0.001 ✅\n- W≥5: NS (dimensionality: 51200 × W features for n=20)\n- W=1: 3/3 Holm-Bonferroni ✅; W=3: 0/3 Bonferroni (null-centered v2); W≥5: NS\n- Layer selection: `bal_acc × crossing_rate` selected L10 (15.6%); threshold-dependent metrics consensus selects L63 (98%); pure `bal_acc` selects L47 (73%, bal_acc=0.8290 vs L63=0.7585) (D036)\n\n**OLD biased-layer results (RETRACTED as metric artifact):**\n| Model | Biased Layer | Corrected Layer | Biased p-value | Corrected p-value |\n|-------|-------------|----------------|----------------|-------------------|\n| R1-32B | L10 (16%) | L63 (98%) | 0.064-0.13 (NS) | <0.001 (W=1) ✅ |\n| QwQ-32B | L2 (3%) | L60 (94%) | 0.35-0.83 (NS) | <0.005 (all W) ✅ |\n\n### 4-Model Holm-Bonferroni Summary (D032 — COMPLETE: 12/12 ✅)\n\n| Model | Arch | Training | Scale | Layer | W | bal_acc | precision | FPR | Selectivity |\n|-------|------|----------|-------|-------|---|--------|-----------|-----|-------------|\n| R1-8B | Llama | R1-distilled | 8B | L14 (45%) | 15 | +8.2pp ✅ | +22.4pp ✅ | -7.4pp ✅ | 12.5pp |\n| OT-7B | Qwen | STILL | 7B | L16 (57%) | 3 | +10.7pp ✅ | +21.9pp ✅ | -17.1pp ✅ | 18.3pp |\n| QwQ-32B | Qwen | native | 32B | L60 (94%) | 3 | +15.4pp ✅ | +23.6pp ✅ | -9.8pp ✅ | 15.3pp |\n| R1-32B | Qwen | R1-distilled | 32B | L63 (98%) | 1 | +18.7pp ✅ | +15.4pp ✅ | -14.6pp ✅ | 7.5pp |\n\n**12/12 all pass Holm-Bonferroni step-down (α=0.05)**. Previously 5/12 with biased layers.\nPrecision advantage remarkably consistent: +15.4 to +23.6pp across all 4 models.\nCaveats: Different W per model; R1-32B W=1 coverage=25%; QwQ lead time negative.\n\n### Position Mediation Analysis (D038 → D039 → D042 complete)\n\n**Finding**: Position (relative step t/T) is a significant component of probe performance. 3/4 models retain HS advantage after residualization; R1-32B is the exception.\n\n| Model | W | Resid HS BA | Resid Text BA | HS-Text Gap | Gap p | HB |\n|-------|---|------------|--------------|-------------|-------|-----|\n| OT-7B | 3 | 0.609 | 0.540 | **+6.9pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n| R1-8B | 15 | 0.669 | 0.605 | **+6.4pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n| R1-8B | 3 | 0.571 | 0.534 | **+3.7pp** | <0.001 | ✅ |\n| QwQ-32B | 3 | 0.619 | 0.582 | **+3.7pp** | 0.011 | ✅ |\n| R1-32B | 1 | 0.552 | 0.532 | +1.9pp | 0.914 | ❌ |\n\nPosition-only BA: OT-7B/R1-8B/QwQ ≈ 0.706; R1-32B = 0.686.\n\n**D042 final picture**: HS advantage has two separable components — position-mediated and non-positional. 3/4 models retain significant non-positional HS advantage (HB pass); R1-32B's advantage is almost entirely position-mediated (drop 20.4pp, residualized gap NS). This is consistent with R1-32B's other caveats (W=1 only significant, 25% coverage).\n\n**Key implications for paper**:\n1. Position is a significant component (12-20pp drop) — universal\n2. 3/4 models retain non-positional HS advantage (residualized BA gap +3.7 to +6.9pp, HB pass)\n3. R1-32B is the exception: HS advantage position-mediated, residualized gap NS\n4. Temporal windowing preserves non-positional signal (R1-8B: 24pp drop@W=3 → 16pp@W=15)\n5. Paper framing: \"HS advantage persists after position removal in 3/4 models; R1-32B advantage is position-mediated\"\n\n### 5-Seed Robustness (D041)\n\n| Model | HB Pass Rate | Mean ΔPrec ± std | Mean ΔBA ± std |\n|-------|-------------|------------------|----------------|\n| OT-7B | **5/5** | +20.9 ± 1.3pp | +11.3 ± 1.5pp |\n| R1-32B | **5/5** | +13.7 ± 2.0pp | +11.8 ± 2.4pp |\n| QwQ-32B | **5/5** | +19.9 ± 2.5pp | +11.4 ± 3.2pp |\n| R1-8B | **3/5** | +14.6 ± 4.5pp | +9.4 ± 2.4pp |\n\nR1-8B failures are FPR-specific (seed 123 FPR p=0.262, seed 456 FPR p=0.952). Precision is directionally consistent across all 20 seed-model combinations (always positive). ΔPrec never reverses.\n\n**D041 insight**: Robustness splits by MODEL not SCALE. R1-32B (5/5, ΔPrec std=2.0pp) is more stable than R1-8B (3/5, ΔPrec std=4.5pp). \"7-8B robust / 32B sample-limited\" is factually wrong. R1-32B's absolute precision std (12.8pp) vs paired delta std (2.0pp) — paper must distinguish these.\n\n**Per-model evidence tier (D042)**:\n- **OT-7B**: Cleanest — 5/5 HB, largest residualized gap (+6.9pp), highest selectivity (18.3pp)\n- **QwQ-32B**: Robust — 5/5 HB, residualized gap holds (+3.7pp), but position baseline competitive\n- **R1-8B**: Precision-robust — residualized holds (+3.7-6.4pp), but FPR unstable (3/5 HB)\n- **R1-32B**: Statistically stable (5/5 HB, ΔPrec std=2.0pp) but advantage position-mediated (residualized NS)\n\n**Residualized precision**: Not tested (scope limited to BA per Reviewer recommendation).\n\n### BA-Layer Robustness: Metric Circularity Refuted (D044)\n\nR13 W1 concern: corrected selection uses threshold-dependent metrics (precision, FPR), evaluation also uses precision/FPR — potential circularity. Test: compute HS vs text on BA-selected layers (threshold-free criterion).\n\n| Model | BA-Opt Layer | ΔPrec | ΔBA | ΔFPR | ΔAUROC | All 4 HB? |\n|-------|-------------|-------|-----|------|--------|-----------|\n| R1-8B | L12 | +17.8pp | +7.8pp | -12.9pp | +9.3pp | ✅ |\n| OT-7B | L9 | +25.4pp | +11.7pp | -19.3pp | +14.8pp | ✅ |\n| QwQ-32B | L30 | +18.0pp | +14.8pp | -8.0pp | +17.3pp | ✅ |\n| R1-32B | L47 | +13.7pp | +14.9pp | -23.1pp | +21.1pp | ✅ |\n\n**4/4 models × 4 metrics = 16/16 HB pass.** HS advantage is a genuine modality property, not a layer selection artifact.\n\nKey insight: R1-32B on BA-layer L47 shows ΔPrec +13.7pp and ΔAUROC +21.1pp — stronger than corrected L63 in threshold-free metrics. OT-7B on BA-layer L9 has ΔPrec +25.4pp > corrected L16 (+21.9pp). HS advantage is robust to layer selection criterion.\n\nCaveat: QwQ FPR adj_p=0.041 (marginal, CI close to zero). Other 15/16 tests p≤0.006.\n\n### Post-hoc Power Analysis (D044)\n\n| Model | n (test) | MDE (80% power, α=0.05) |\n|-------|----------|------------------------|\n| OT-7B | 47-69 | 6.7-8.1pp |\n| R1-8B | 43-63 | 7.4-9.0pp |\n| QwQ-32B | 29 | 9.5pp |\n| R1-32B | 20-30 | 8.6-11.2pp |\n\nAll significant effects (15-24pp) are well above MDE → adequately powered. R1-32B residualized gap (+1.9pp) is far below MDE (11.2pp) → NS is power limitation, not evidence of absence.\n\n### Negative Results (expanded with R3 supplementary experiments)\n- **BOCPD/CUSUM (4/4 models)**: R1-8B BOCPD 93% detection but lead +3.5 < threshold +4.9; OT-7B/R1-32B/QwQ all 0% detection across all λ. CUSUM worse than threshold on all models.\n- **Mahalanobis (4/4 models confirmed negative)**: R1-8B (+0.07), OT-7B (+0.031), R1-32B (+0.148), QwQ (+0.204) — all separation ≈ 0. Signal in minor PCA components, not principal directions.\n- **RepE direction probing (4/4 models, corrected layers confirmed)**: Direction-based supervised method (needs CP labels). Results highly layer-dependent and model-specific:\n  - R1-32B L63 (corrected): bal_acc=0.559 (near-random), FPR=49.9% — **direction vector fails at deep layer** where supervised LR excels (0.826). Train-test gap 13.3pp shows poor generalization.\n  - QwQ L60 (corrected): bal_acc=0.756, precision=0.512, FPR=0.309 — **improves** from L2 (0.666), narrows gap with supervised LR W=1 (0.740 bal_acc), but still inferior in precision/FPR.\n  - R1-8B L14: bal_acc=0.749, OT-7B L16: bal_acc=0.642\n  - **Key insight**: Supervised LR is necessary — mean-difference direction cannot decode safety commitment at deep layers for R1-32B (discriminative training finds signal that simple direction averaging misses). Layer selection sensitivity applies to RepE too, but in model-specific ways (R1-32B: shallow better for RepE; QwQ: deep better for both).\n- **MLP nonlinear probe (4/4 models)**: 3/4 models worse than LR. Linear probes sufficient; nonlinearity adds no value.\n- **CCS-adapted (Burns et al. 2023, 4/4 models)**: WEAKLY SUPERVISED (needs CP labels for pair construction, not truly unsupervised). R1-8B bal_acc=0.777 (between supervised LR 0.817 and RepE 0.749). R1-32B FPR=0.410 (near-chance). OT-7B precision=0.319 (near-chance, high lead=20.5 is artifact of high FPR). Uses scheme B layers (biased). Paper must: (a) label as \"weakly supervised\" not \"unsupervised\"; (b) disclose pair construction differs from Burns et al.; (c) note scheme B layer limitation.\n- **Cross-model transfer (exp-003)**: All directions fail entirely (best: 58.3% acc, 40.7% crossing).\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **EMNLP LLM Security track fit**: Strong — defense/detection evaluation for reasoning model jailbreak.\n- **Method simplicity risk**: Mitigate: frame as empirical study. Contribution is systematic evaluation + layer selection sensitivity discovery + comprehensive negative results.\n- **Statistical power**: With corrected layers, **12/12** tests pass Holm-Bonferroni across ALL 4 models (up from 5/12 with biased layers).\n- **HS advantage universal**: UPGRADED from \"scale-dependent\" — layer selection is the true moderator, not scale. Cleaner story.\n- **Trace vs step FPR**: Both reported with explanation.\n- **High safe FPR risk**: All methods 39-62% safe FPR. Frame as diagnostic tool limitation.\n- **32B caveats**: HS advantage exists but is more sensitive to window size (R1-32B W=1 only) and affected by dimensionality (51200-d at large W with n=20). Lead times shorter than 7-8B. These are honest limitations, not disqualifiers.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. \"Method novelty?\" → Empirical study + systematic method comparison + layer selection sensitivity as methodological contribution + comprehensive negative results (6 methods fail).\n2. \"Only one model family?\" → **RESOLVED**: 4 models, 2 architectures (Llama + Qwen), 2 training methods, 2 scales. ALL showing significant HS advantage at corrected layers.\n3. \"GRU unstable?\" → 3-seed reporting with worst-seed bounds. R1-32B GRU at L10 was unstable; needs re-evaluation at L63.\n4. \"Too few traces?\" → Cross-model validation + control task selectivity 7.5-18.5pp.\n5. \"Fine-grained taxonomy?\" → Out of scope for current study.\n6. \"HS doesn't beat text?\" → **QUALIFIED REBUTTAL (D031)**: HS outperforms text at correct layers with STRONG evidence at 7-8B (precision +22pp, Holm-Bonf) and QUALIFIED evidence at 32B (R1-32B: significant W=1 but narrow; QwQ: significant all W but late detection). 32B non-significance at OLD layers was artifact. Layer selection sensitivity analysis shows this is a methodological issue, not absence of signal.\n7. \"Commitment point circular?\" → Cross-model consistency + control task selectivity argues against artifact.\n8. \"Missing related work?\" → Expansion to 30+ citations.\n9. \"No FPR analysis?\" → RESOLVED: both trace-level and step-level FPR reported.\n10. \"High safe FPR?\" → Limitation acknowledged.\n11. \"Control task / position confound?\" → RESOLVED (C2, D011): selectivity 7.5-18.5pp, HS FPR < position-only FPR.\n12. \"Multiple testing correction?\" → **RESOLVED**: 12/12 Holm-Bonferroni step-down (α=0.05) across all 4 models (up from 5/12 with biased layers).\n13. \"Trace vs step FPR?\" → Both reported with explanation.\n14. \"Layer selection is just hyperparameter tuning?\" → No — we show a systematic bias in a commonly used composite metric. The ablation across 5 metrics × 4 models is a reproducible methodological finding, not a one-off parameter choice.\n15. \"Why not just use the best layer for each model?\" → We do. The point is that the METRIC for selecting \"best\" matters. Biased metrics produce systematically wrong selections, masking real effects.\n16. \"32B results are marginal / only W=1 significant for R1-32B?\" → Dimensionality constraint (51200 × W > n=20 at W≥5). QwQ L60 significant at ALL W values. R1-32B L63 significant at W=1. Both confirm HS advantage exists; practical deployment would use W=1-3 for 32B models.\n\n## Title Candidates (D031)\n- \"Layer Selection Matters: How Metric Choice Determines Hidden-State Probe Effectiveness for Safety Monitoring\"\n- \"Temporal Probing for Safety Commitment Detection in Reasoning Models: A Comprehensive Evaluation\"\n- \"What Detects Safety Commitment in Reasoning Models? A Systematic Comparison of Probe-Based Methods\"\n- \"Hidden-State vs Text Monitoring for Reasoning Model Safety: Layer Selection as the Missing Variable\"\n","numLines":323,"startLine":1,"totalLines":323}}}
